lers/BPHomebrewViewController.m\n75fc0eb1e12aa38ea77447e702d2d78edfe8a1bb35f6eda365bb8a44b464196f  Cakebrew.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj\n9d89d375ad61bea333cc8d11f7226b109a15810c5e359607b23e903666e5c1e8  CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m\n\nThe other four refactor files byte-compare equal to the protected original. Whole staged/unstaged/untracked workspace inspected, index empty, git diff --check passes, no scratch artifacts in either worktree. No app/UI/full-suite runs, preferences/cache changes or host remediation attempted.\n\n## Independent gates\n\nFull verification, UI review and expert review remain primary-agent responsibilities. This handoff does not approve those gates or the implementation itself.\n\n## Final focused GREEN and startup limitation\n\nThe ordinary xcodebuild green attempt compiled the one-line fix without warning/error, but never entered any test body. At the primary agent's five-minute startup cutoff, a one-second sample of exact owned xctest PID24333 showed the main thread in XCTestDriver _prepareTestConfigurationAndIDESession -> XCTFuture _waitForFulfillmentSync -> XCTWaiter, not a product test. See xctest-startup.sample.txt:25-37. Sent SIGINT only to owned xcodebuild PID21926, which exited75 with TEST INTERRUPTED (green.log). No retry of xcodebuild was performed. Its owned PIDs21926,21958,21977,24333 were confirmed gone before any alternative run. No host daemons or configuration were touched.\n\nOne authorized alternative focused TDD instrument then ran the actual compiled XCTest bundle directly:\n\n/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/xctest -XCTest BPSearchCoordinatorTests /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-clear-fix.fdjddj/DerivedData/Build/Products/Debug/CakebrewTests.xctest\n\ndirect-xctest.log contains all EIGHT named test cases, including both new clear-search regressions, each observed started and passed. Total eight tests, zero failures, 0.157 s, command exit0. This provides focused GREEN evidence using the real committed test source and compiled production code; it is not a replacement for the full xcodebuild verification gate. No source changes after this pass, and no further refactoring was needed beyond the minimal one-line change.\n\nNo UI-target compilation or UI/app/full-suite run was attempted in this separate fix assignment. The primary agent retained display ownership for other work. A supplemental harness was briefly drafted as an alternative in this temporary evidence directory, but never compiled/executed and removed once direct XCTest worked. No harness artifacts remain.\n\nAll owned test commands/processes have exited. Source remains frozen at the hashes above. Standard full verification and independent gates are still outstanding.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788824197919,"completed_at_ms":1788824198167}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:36:38.288Z","ordinal":19755,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07e3b-1c90-7cb0-a40e-68aa08a21958","call_id":"call_pxOiuBU2Wro3KAs8fVe16BAf","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e11a48\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.24707545,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3108,\"output\":\" .github/workflows/ci.yml                   | 6 ++++++\\n AGENTS.md                                  | 5 +++++\\n Cakebrew/de.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\\n Cakebrew/fr.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\\n Cakebrew/it.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\\n Cakebrew/pt.lproj/Localizable.strings      | 1 -\\n Cakebrew/zh-Hans.lproj/Localizable.strings | 1 -\\n 7 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\\n Cakebrew.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj              | 14 ++++++\\n Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m | 59 +++++++++++--------------\\n CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m               | 19 ++++++--\\n 3 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)\\n Cakebrew.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj              | 14 ++++++\\n Cakebrew/Controllers/BPHomebrewViewController.m | 59 +++++++++++--------------\\n CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m               | 19 ++++++--\\n 3 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)\\n# Independent #142 bounded UI review — APPROVED\\n\\nReviewed the entire branch/workspace diff and all untracked files under `.worktrees/issue-142-l10n` against main/HEAD after reading its complete AGENTS.md and cakebrew-ui-review. No source edits or commits. Source hash before and after: `c39d734d72e5298ba5ea7d4a7a4f2ccb8812d48d285475e63ef6a430ab743064`.\\n\\nNo actionable UI findings in this slice. Approval covers the restored Formulae translations, native presentation/accessibility, and report presentation; it is NOT full verification or a passing UI journey suite.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- Isolated Debug build: `xcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew -configuration Debug -destination 'platform=macOS' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/cakebrew-142-ui.Bwegyu/DerivedData CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`. Host build passed in 13.824s; no warning/error lines. Initial sandbox attempt exited 66 before loading the existing valid workspace, with CoreSimulator/XPC errors; no source/config change used to overcome it.\\n- Display unlocked before launch (`IOConsoleLocked = No`). Exclusive display/app/preferences/cache ownership granted by root. No XCUITest launched or retried.\\n- Serialized exact temporary mock executable, `-BPMockBrew -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier '' -AppleLanguages '(locale)'`, for de/fr/it/pt/zh-Hans. Runtime `NSBundle.mainBundle.preferredLocalizations` confirmed each requested locale, recorded in `*-light-debugger.log`. Exact owned PIDs: de24710, fr25940, it26542, pt26791, zh-Hans27006.\\n- Native app-open-URLs flow: `open -a <exact temporary app> <temporary Brewfile>` containing only `brew 'mockwget'` and `cask 'mockchrome'`. Review sheet presented without confirming installation. Mock fixture rows/badges verified in AX and screenshots. No real Homebrew/package operations.\\n- Correct table AX descriptions and review section headings: de `Formeln`, fr `Formules`, it `Formule`, pt `Fórmulas`, zh-Hans unchanged `Formulae`. Main/review AX dumps for each locale preserve `brewfile.review.entries` and sidebar stable identifiers. Native AXTextArea exposes full readable review text; native sheet and buttons remain intact.\\n- Visually inspected ten app-window-only PNGs: `de/fr/it/pt/zh-Hans-system.png` (actual system Dark Aqua) and matching `*-aqua.png`. Restored headings fit comfortably, no truncation/clipping/overlap or contrast regression. Sidebar badges retain expected mock counts. Existing long French/Italian sidebar strings abbreviate with ellipsis; their keys/layout are unchanged by this slice and full AX descriptions remain available.\\n- Opposite-appearance check was a diagnostic-only temporary `NSApp.appearance = NSAppearance(named: NSAppearanceNameAqua)` through LLDB against the exact owned PID, detached before capture; original appearance was nil and restored to nil. No global appearance or language settings changed. This is not evidence of physical typing, menu navigation, or UI-journey execution.\\n- Review sheets cancelled via existing AppKit endSheet returnCode1001, then owned apps quit normally; no install confirmation. First German cancellation diagnostic had a compile-only expression error for untyped attachedSheet; explicit NSWindow cast corrected it. No product change. A capture helper initially stopped when the French window was not yet on-screen; existing mock was retained, readiness verified, then capture continued. Neither event was a failed application test.\\n- Report reviewed from real Markdown output plus renderer: semantic heading hierarchy and labeled summary table; counts distinguish confirmed placeholders, intentional English, unreviewed equality, different, missing, and extra. Informational/non-blocking nature and non-quality nature of Different explicitly stated. Sorted, escaped key lists provide exact actionable identities without color-dependent meaning. JSON alternative available. Report is lengthy by design; no actionable presentation problem. GitHub's live rendering/assistive-technology implementation was not exercised, because no PR/job publication is authorized in this review.\\n\\n## State restoration and limitations\\n\\nFresh backup immediately before first launch contained six persistent preference keys, not an older run's backup. After every owned mock had exited, exact persistent domain restored and independently re-read in a fresh process: six keys equal. Cache restored byte-for-byte, SHA256 `01c1e93bc5bc2541d18a2d5711497c2290c13a0163d269d510bc2ae15a016df0`. Backups retained here as evidence. Temporary Brewfile and helper source/input scripts removed after completion; no scratch files added to the repository. No installed app modified and no unrelated processes terminated.\\n\\nNative regression evidence in implementer handoff covers runtime resource values. Existing Brewfile journey `testBrewfileReviewShowsGroupedStatusesAndCancelRunsNothing` covers grouped review/cancel, but was not run here. Previously reported XCTest initialization failures remain unresolved and must not be described as UI test passes. Complete verification and subsequent independent code review remain separate gates.\\n# Separate queued-search cancellation fix\\n\\nWorktree: /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation\\nBranch: fix/search-clear-cancellation. Base: 8263716 plus the primary agent's uncommitted copy of the frozen #143 refactor.\\n\\nOwned and changed ONLY Cakebrew/Controllers/BPSearchCoordinator.m and CakebrewTests/BPSearchCoordinatorTests.m relative to that refactor. No commit, staging, push or PR.\\n\\n## Separate TDD evidence\\n\\nAdded two regression tests first, before changing production code:\\n\\n- testClearingSearchInvalidatesRetainedCallbackWithoutResumingSearch schedules work, clears search before manually firing the retained block, then asserts zero searches and no resumed search state. The injected search action simulates delivering results so the state assertion proves the stale work cannot reopen search.\\n- testNewQueryRunsAfterClearingWithoutRevivingOlderQuery queues an old query, clears, queues a fresh query, explicitly executes both retained callbacks, and requires only the fresh query to run. Its results can start a new session and restore its sidebar row normally.\\n\\nRED: red.log:1605-1618 contains four expected assertion failures across the two new tests: performed=1 instead of0, searching unexpectedly true, stale query still executing after a new query, and performed containing old plus new instead of new only. All six original coordinator tests passed. Eight tests executed, four assertion failures, xcodebuild exit65. This is an observed behavioral regression failure, not a compile or runner error.\\n\\nMinimal fix: increment generation once at the start of endSearchReturningSidebarRow, before canceling in-flight manager work and returning the saved sidebar row. Existing queued callbacks already compare their captured generation. No extra scheduler, rendering, manager, toolbar, sidebar, UI, or state-restoration changes.\\n\\nGREEN status and command completion are recorded in the final section below; do not assume green from the source change alone.\\n\\nFocused command: xcodebuild test -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme CakebrewTests -destination 'platform=macOS' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-clear-fix.fdjddj/DerivedData -only-testing:CakebrewTests/BPSearchCoordinatorTests CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO.\\n\\n## Frozen scope and hashes\\n\\nfix-only.patch contains exactly the two-file delta: one production line and42 test lines. It applies cleanly with git apply --check to the original refactor worktree; its reverse applies cleanly to this fix worktree. Dry-run checks only, neither application performed.\\n\\nFix-only patch SHA256: 51601f23a2843677e83acccef8a7a32bf9570f4f5e9e9c6cfa868b42270a6c88\\n\\nCombined full source SHA256: 3770617bd4179ccb8dd50761b5cf9b33730589c5591dae1e1016a06becad8daa\\n\\nFull source hashing uses git diff HEAD --binary bytes, then sorted untracked paths, each newline + path + newline + exact file bytes.\\n\\nOriginal protected refactor full source SHA256: 724a7568797d88086da992df60a5faecd36bc5fa6184d78dc1b79b6a4bfd7e6b. Tracked binary diff remains141772a5c54686ceb1213c5113d5b34e6d1c8898a234429c0e2c121035ae9b93 in both worktrees because the fix changes only two currently untracked files. Original refactor is untouched.\\n\\nCombined file inventory:\\n\\n0082906f340ee9c54a7878131c329142642f2a130f5c22faba99d2d64288d687  Cakebrew/Controllers/BPSearch