{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T23:46:24.599Z","ordinal":20058,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6f36c0a5-cc63-433d-89e3-52ee3d628e2b","process_id":"15623","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/review.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/review.md","name":"review.md","path":"/private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/review.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Search UI gates — 2026-09-07\n\nIndependent review using complete AGENTS.md and cakebrew-ui-review. Reviewed branch plus staged/unstaged/untracked diff; no repository source edits, staging, commits, or publication. Runtime lease released to root after exact restoration.\n\n## Decisions and prioritized findings\n\n1. **P2, fix slice gate finding: missing queued-clear UI regression journey.** `CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m` has cask search and notification navigation/cancellation journeys but none that exercises clear via `BPToolbar` submission / `performSearchWithString:@\"\"` / `endSearchReturningSidebarRow`. Existing notification tests call `cancelForNavigation`, a different coordinator method. The two new unit tests prove the generation guard but do not cover the changed controller-to-rendering integration. Under AGENTS' behavior-journey rule, add a deterministic CI-safe mock queue-then-clear action and a journey that verifies empty field, expected destination rows, and no late mockvscode result beyond the debounce interval. Start from Installed Formulae to test the authorized pending-debounce fix without broadening to completed-cask restoration. Observe red/mutation bite, restore green, then rerun invalidated gates. Routed to root/implementer; reviewer did not fix it.\n\n2. **P2, separate pre-existing observation (not a regression or scope expansion): completed search can leave stale results after same-row clear.** On All Casks, complete mockvscode search, then call the ordinary clear entry point after pending work finishes. Field becomes empty, coordinator reports searching=0, sidebar remains `sidebar.casks.all`, but the table still contains only mockvscode, not the full cask list. Expected: the destination's complete list returns after clear. Reproduced on the behavior-only original slice as well as the fix mock; original controller rendering logic is unchanged from main. `endSearchAndCleanup` at BPHomebrewViewController.m:843 reselects the already selected row without explicitly rebuilding the table. This is a likely explanation, not a separate implemented fix. Evidence: `refactor-clear-only-debugger.log` (searching=0), `refactor-clear-only-ax.txt`, `refactor-clear-only.png`; fix comparison `fix-cleared-ax.txt`. Actual inspection invoked existing controller methods through LLDB, not physical mouse typing. Root explicitly kept this separate from the pending-debounce task.\n\n**Original behavior-only extraction UI gate: APPROVED.** No actionable UI regression from that slice; eight applicable journeys passed and actual search surfaces checked in Aqua/Dark Aqua with stable accessibility identity and badges. The existing clear limitations are not claimed fixed.\n\n**Search-clear fix UI gate: NOT APPROVED until finding 1 is resolved.** Bounded visual inspection passed; this is a coverage finding, not an observed generation-guard failure. No extra eight-journey batch run on the fix once its source needed changes.\n\n## Source identities\n\nBase HEAD/main 826371682a2044ea9cf8a95fdc4ac63804737b09. No staged changes.\n\n- `.worktrees/issue-143-search`, refactor/search-coordinator, full SHA256 before/after `724a7568797d88086da992df60a5faecd36bc5fa6184d78dc1b79b6a4bfd7e6b`.\n- `.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation`, fix/search-clear-cancellation, full SHA256 before/after `3770617bd4179ccb8dd50761b5cf9b33730589c5591dae1e1016a06becad8daa`.\n- Hash input is binary `git diff HEAD` plus sorted untracked paths and exact bytes. The fix differs from original only by one coordinator generation increment and two unit tests.\n\n## Executed automated evidence\n\n- Original exact recent isolated build reused from `/private/tmp/cakebrew-xcode-closed-retry.yrQJ4u/DerivedData`; its handoff and unchanged full source hash checked. That build-for-testing was warning-free and had already passed the strengthened cask-search journey. No stale arbitrary app reuse.\n- Separate fix compiled with `xcodebuild build-for-testing -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/FixDerivedData CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='-' CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM='' PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=''`. `fix-compile.log`: TEST BUILD SUCCEEDED, 18.853s, no warning/error diagnostics.\n- Original `caffeinate -dimsu xcodebuild test-without-building -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS'`, exact recent DD above, result bundle `refactor-focused.xcresult`, same signing arguments, eight `-only-testing:CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests/<name>` selections below. Actual named starts/passes verified in `refactor-focused.log`; exit0, 8 tests, 0 failures, 153.946s (command155.440s). No UI initialization timeout or product assertion failure. Nonfatal IDELaunchParametersSnapshot debugger-version diagnostics appeared, as in the previous successful run.\n\nExecuted names and durations:\n\n- testCaskNotificationCancelsPendingSearch — 17.077s\n- testCaskNotificationLeavesSearchForOutdatedDestination — 19.754s\n- testCaskNotificationLeavesSearchOnAlreadySelectedDestination — 23.817s\n- testFormulaeNotificationCancelsPendingSearch — 16.724s\n- testFormulaeNotificationLeavesSearchForOutdatedDestination — 19.587s\n- testFormulaeNotificationLeavesSearchOnAlreadySelectedDestination — 23.710s\n- testSearchFieldIsAvailable — 10.112s\n- testSearchingFindsCasksAndKeepsTheSidebarSelection — 23.166s\n\nThese test actual mock result arrival/removal, namespace-correct destinations, same-row notification refresh, pending debounce invalidation, nonzero search geometry/enabled state, and stable sidebar identity. Not a full suite/verification gate.\n\n## Actual visual and accessibility evidence\n\nLaunched exact temporary app bundles with `-BPMockBrew -BPMockWarmNotificationTarget casks -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier ''`. Original owned PIDs41636 and43751; fix42968. Used existing `beginMockNotificationSearch:` action after selecting All Casks row10 (enum checked); debounced mockvscode result actually rendered. No package install/upgrade/remove, real brew, installed app replacement, or global appearance/language change.\n\nInspected app-window-only screenshots:\n\n- Original `refactor-results-dark.png` is **Aqua despite its early filename**; it is the actual native system appearance this session. Correct dark evidence is `refactor-results-actual-dark.png`, visibly Dark Aqua. Original selected All Casks, readable mockvscode/name/status, native search/cancel control, spacing and mock badges intact. `refactor-results-aqua.png` additionally captures explicit Aqua.\n- Fix `fix-results-system.png` is Aqua; `fix-results-dark.png` is explicit Dark Aqua. Same search layout/content, no clipping/overlap or changed badge counts. Fix window was inactive during captures, so native dimmed chrome/inactive selection is expected; original screenshots also cover active window presentation.\n- Native AX dumps alongside screenshots show AXSearchField value mockvscode and327x38 geometry, selected stable `sidebar.casks.all`, and full sidebar descriptions with counts (formula installed3, outdated1, all4, leaves1, pinned1, repositories2; cask installed2/outdated1/all3). UI rows remain on cell text fields, no new AX identity changes. No VoiceOver speech or physical keyboard test claimed.\n- Appearance temporarily set via bounded LLDB `NSApp.appearance` to Aqua/DarkAqua and restored to original nil before each app quit. Actual `effectiveAppearance` recorded for Dark Aqua. No OS appearance preference mutation.\n- Initial debugger-only search expressions failed compilation due missing return-type knowledge for KVC; cast message return types as LLDB requested, then actual selector invocation succeeded. These were temporary diagnostic expressions, not product/test failures. All debuggers detached; no instrumentation entered source.\n\n## Coordination and exact state restoration\n\nInitial inspection found unrelated ControlPlane xcodebuild PID34993. It was left untouched; runtime launch held until it exited. Only isolated compilation/static review occurred concurrently. Display unlocked. First preliminary snapshot was not used for restoration; a **new snapshot in runtime-state/** was taken immediately before actual UI test/app launch.\n\nAfter every owned mock/runner/debugger exited, restored `com.scottdensmore.Cakebrew` persistent-domain envelope and the exact fresh cache bytes. Independent new Swift process reported `fresh-process preference dictionary equality: true; cache exact: true`. Cache backup SHA256 `01c1e93bc5bc2541d18a2d5711497c2290c13a0163d269d510bc2ae15a016df0`. Original app appearance nil restored for all owned mock lifetimes. Exact process-name inspection found no Cakebrew/xcodebuild/LLDB remaining; final command's exit1 was the expected final no-match pgrep, not restoration failure.\n\nEvidence/helper sources are isolated under this /private/tmp directory, nothing added to the repository. No user source/config changes touched. Source hashes checked unchanged after runtime release. Full verification and expert review remain separate gates.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Search UI gates — 2026-09-07\n\nIndependent review using complete AGENTS.md and cakebrew-ui-review. Reviewed branch plus staged/unstaged/untracked diff; no repository source edits, staging, commits, or publication. Runtime lease released to root after exact restoration.\n\n## Decisions and prioritized findings\n\n1. **P2, fix slice gate finding: missing queued-clear UI regression journey.** `CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m` has cask search and notification navigation/cancellation journeys but none that exercises clear via `BPToolbar` submission / `performSearchWithString:@\"\"` / `endSearchReturningSidebarRow`. Existing notification tests call `cancelForNavigation`, a different coordinator method. The two new unit tests prove the generation guard but do not cover the changed controller-to-rendering integration. Under AGENTS' behavior-journey rule, add a deterministic CI-safe mock queue-then-clear action and a journey that verifies empty field, expected destination rows, and no late mockvscode result beyond the debounce interval. Start from Installed Formulae to test the authorized pending-debounce fix without broadening to completed-cask restoration. Observe red/mutation bite, restore green, then rerun invalidated gates. Routed to root/implementer; reviewer did not fix it.\n\n2. **P2, separate pre-existing observation (not a regression or scope expansion): completed search can leave stale results after same-row clear.** On All Casks, complete mockvscode search, then call the ordinary clear entry point after pending work finishes. Field becomes empty, coordinator reports searching=0, sidebar remains `sidebar.casks.all`, but the table still contains only mockvscode, not the full cask list. Expected: the destination's complete list returns after clear. Reproduced on the behavior-only original slice as well as the fix mock; original controller rendering logic is unchanged from main. `endSearchAndCleanup` at BPHomebrewViewController.m:843 reselects the already selected row without explicitly rebuilding the table. This is a likely explanation, not a separate implemented fix. Evidence: `refactor-clear-only-debugger.log` (searching=0), `refactor-clear-only-ax.txt`, `refactor-clear-only.png`; fix comparison `fix-cleared-ax.txt`. Actual inspection invoked existing controller methods through LLDB, not physical mouse typing. Root explicitly kept this separate from the pending-debounce task.\n\n**Original behavior-only extraction UI gate: APPROVED.** No actionable UI regression from that slice; eight applicable journeys passed and actual search surfaces checked in Aqua/Dark Aqua with stable accessibility identity and badges. The existing clear limitations are not claimed fixed.\n\n**Search-clear fix UI gate: NOT APPROVED until finding 1 is resolved.** Bounded visual inspection passed; this is a coverage finding, not an observed generation-guard failure. No extra eight-journey batch run on the fix once its source needed changes.\n\n## Source identities\n\nBase HEAD/main 826371682a2044ea9cf8a95fdc4ac63804737b09. No staged changes.\n\n- `.worktrees/issue-143-search`, refactor/search-coordinator, full SHA256 before/after `724a7568797d88086da992df60a5faecd36bc5fa6184d78dc1b79b6a4bfd7e6b`.\n- `.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation`, fix/search-clear-cancellation, full SHA256 before/after `3770617bd4179ccb8dd50761b5cf9b33730589c5591dae1e1016a06becad8daa`.\n- Hash input is binary `git diff HEAD` plus sorted untracked paths and exact bytes. The fix differs from original only by one coordinator generation increment and two unit tests.\n\n## Executed automated evidence\n\n- Original exact recent isolated build reused from `/private/tmp/cakebrew-xcode-closed-retry.yrQJ4u/DerivedData`; its handoff and unchanged full source hash checked. That build-for-testing was warning-free and had already passed the strengthened cask-search journey. No stale arbitrary app reuse.\n- Separate fix compiled with `xcodebuild build-for-testing -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/FixDerivedData CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='-' CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM='' PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=''`. `fix-compile.log`: TEST BUILD SUCCEEDED, 18.853s, no warning/error diagnostics.\n- Original `caffeinate -dimsu xcodebuild test-without-building -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS'`, exact recent DD above, result bundle `refactor-focused.xcresult`, same signing arguments, eight `-only-testing:CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests/<name>` selections below. Actual named starts/passes verified in `refactor-focused.log`; exit0, 8 tests, 0 failures, 153.946s (command155.440s). No UI initialization timeout or product assertion failure. Nonfatal IDELaunchParametersSnapshot debugger-version diagnostics appeared, as in the previous successful run.\n\nExecuted names and durations:\n\n- testCaskNotificationCancelsPendingSearch — 17.077s\n- testCaskNotificationLeavesSearchForOutdatedDestination — 19.754s\n- testCaskNotificationLeavesSearchOnAlreadySelectedDestination — 23.817s\n- testFormulaeNotificationCancelsPendingSearch — 16.724s\n- testFormulaeNotificationLeavesSearchForOutdatedDestination — 19.587s\n- testFormulaeNotificationLeavesSearchOnAlreadySelectedDestination — 23.710s\n- testSearchFieldIsAvailable — 10.112s\n- testSearchingFindsCasksAndKeepsTheSidebarSelection — 23.166s\n\nThese test actual mock result arrival/removal, namespace-correct destinations, same-row notification refresh, pending debounce invalidation, nonzero search geometry/enabled state, and stable sidebar identity. Not a full suite/verification gate.\n\n## Actual visual and accessibility evidence\n\nLaunched exact temporary app bundles with `-BPMockBrew -BPMockWarmNotificationTarget casks -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier ''`. Original owned PIDs41636 and43751; fix42968. Used existing `beginMockNotificationSearch:` action after selecting All Casks row10 (enum checked); debounced mockvscode result actually rendered. No package install/upgrade/remove, real brew, installed app replacement, or global appearance/language change.\n\nInspected app-window-only screenshots:\n\n- Original `refactor-results-dark.png` is **Aqua despite its early filename**; it is the actual native system appearance this session. Correct dark evidence is `refactor-results-actual-dark.png`, visibly Dark Aqua. Original selected All Casks, readable mockvscode/name/status, native search/cancel control, spacing and mock badges intact. `refactor-results-aqua.png` additionally captures explicit Aqua.\n- Fix `fix-results-system.png` is Aqua; `fix-results-dark.png` is explicit Dark Aqua. Same search layout/content, no clipping/overlap or changed badge counts. Fix window was inactive during captures, so native dimmed chrome/inactive selection is expected; original screenshots also cover active window presentation.\n- Native AX dumps alongside screenshots show AXSearchField value mockvscode and327x38 geometry, selected stable `sidebar.casks.all`, and full sidebar descriptions with counts (formula installed3, outdated1, all4, leaves1, pinned1, repositories2; cask installed2/outdated1/all3). UI rows remain on cell text fields, no new AX identity changes. No VoiceOver speech or physical keyboard test claimed.\n- Appearance temporarily set via bounded LLDB `NSApp.appearance` to Aqua/DarkAqua and restored to original nil before each app quit. Actual `effectiveAppearance` recorded for Dark Aqua. No OS appearance preference mutation.\n- Initial debugger-only search expressions failed compilation due missing return-type knowledge for KVC; cast message return types as LLDB requested, then actual selector invocation succeeded. These were temporary diagnostic expressions, not product/test failures. All debuggers detached; no instrumentation entered source.\n\n## Coordination and exact state restoration\n\nInitial inspection found unrelated ControlPlane xcodebuild PID34993. It was left untouched; runtime launch held until it exited. Only isolated compilation/static review occurred concurrently. Display unlocked. First preliminary snapshot was not used for restoration; a **new snapshot in runtime-state/** was taken immediately before actual UI test/app launch.\n\nAfter every owned mock/runner/debugger exited, restored `com.scottdensmore.Cakebrew` persistent-domain envelope and the exact fresh cache bytes. Independent new Swift process reported `fresh-process preference dictionary equality: true; cache exact: true`. Cache backup SHA256 `01c1e93bc5bc2541d18a2d5711497c2290c13a0163d269d510bc2ae15a016df0`. Original app appearance nil restored for all owned mock lifetimes. Exact process-name inspection found no Cakebrew/xcodebuild/LLDB remaining; final command's exit1 was the expected final no-match pgrep, not restoration failure.\n\nEvidence/helper sources are isolated under this /private/tmp directory, nothing added to the repository. No user source/config changes touched. Source hashes checked unchanged after runtime release. Full verification and expert review remain separate gates.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3942},"formatted_output":"# Search UI gates — 2026-09-07\n\nIndependent review using complete AGENTS.md and cakebrew-ui-review. Reviewed branch plus staged/unstaged/untracked diff; no repository source edits, staging, commits, or publication. Runtime lease released to root after exact restoration.\n\n## Decisions and prioritized findings\n\n1. **P2, fix slice gate finding: missing queued-clear UI regression journey.** `CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests.m` has cask search and notification navigation/cancellation journeys but none that exercises clear via `BPToolbar` submission / `performSearchWithString:@\"\"` / `endSearchReturningSidebarRow`. Existing notification tests call `cancelForNavigation`, a different coordinator method. The two new unit tests prove the generation guard but do not cover the changed controller-to-rendering integration. Under AGENTS' behavior-journey rule, add a deterministic CI-safe mock queue-then-clear action and a journey that verifies empty field, expected destination rows, and no late mockvscode result beyond the debounce interval. Start from Installed Formulae to test the authorized pending-debounce fix without broadening to completed-cask restoration. Observe red/mutation bite, restore green, then rerun invalidated gates. Routed to root/implementer; reviewer did not fix it.\n\n2. **P2, separate pre-existing observation (not a regression or scope expansion): completed search can leave stale results after same-row clear.** On All Casks, complete mockvscode search, then call the ordinary clear entry point after pending work finishes. Field becomes empty, coordinator reports searching=0, sidebar remains `sidebar.casks.all`, but the table still contains only mockvscode, not the full cask list. Expected: the destination's complete list returns after clear. Reproduced on the behavior-only original slice as well as the fix mock; original controller rendering logic is unchanged from main. `endSearchAndCleanup` at BPHomebrewViewController.m:843 reselects the already selected row without explicitly rebuilding the table. This is a likely explanation, not a separate implemented fix. Evidence: `refactor-clear-only-debugger.log` (searching=0), `refactor-clear-only-ax.txt`, `refactor-clear-only.png`; fix comparison `fix-cleared-ax.txt`. Actual inspection invoked existing controller methods through LLDB, not physical mouse typing. Root explicitly kept this separate from the pending-debounce task.\n\n**Original behavior-only extraction UI gate: APPROVED.** No actionable UI regression from that slice; eight applicable journeys passed and actual search surfaces checked in Aqua/Dark Aqua with stable accessibility identity and badges. The existing clear limitations are not claimed fixed.\n\n**Search-clear fix UI gate: NOT APPROVED until finding 1 is resolved.** Bounded visual inspection passed; this is a coverage finding, not an observed generation-guard failure. No extra eight-journey batch run on the fix once its source needed changes.\n\n## Source identities\n\nBase HEAD/main 826371682a2044ea9cf8a95fdc4ac63804737b09. No staged changes.\n\n- `.worktrees/issue-143-search`, refactor/search-coordinator, full SHA256 before/after `724a7568797d88086da992df60a5faecd36bc5fa6184d78dc1b79b6a4bfd7e6b`.\n- `.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation`, fix/search-clear-cancellation, full SHA256 before/after `3770617bd4179ccb8dd50761b5cf9b33730589c5591dae1e1016a06becad8daa`.\n- Hash input is binary `git diff HEAD` plus sorted untracked paths and exact bytes. The fix differs from original only by one coordinator generation increment and two unit tests.\n\n## Executed automated evidence\n\n- Original exact recent isolated build reused from `/private/tmp/cakebrew-xcode-closed-retry.yrQJ4u/DerivedData`; its handoff and unchanged full source hash checked. That build-for-testing was warning-free and had already passed the strengthened cask-search journey. No stale arbitrary app reuse.\n- Separate fix compiled with `xcodebuild build-for-testing -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' -derivedDataPath /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/FixDerivedData CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY='-' CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM='' PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=''`. `fix-compile.log`: TEST BUILD SUCCEEDED, 18.853s, no warning/error diagnostics.\n- Original `caffeinate -dimsu xcodebuild test-without-building -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS'`, exact recent DD above, result bundle `refactor-focused.xcresult`, same signing arguments, eight `-only-testing:CakebrewUITests/CakebrewUITests/<name>` selections below. Actual named starts/passes verified in `refactor-focused.log`; exit0, 8 tests, 0 failures, 153.946s (command155.440s). No UI initialization timeout or product assertion failure. Nonfatal IDELaunchParametersSnapshot debugger-version diagnostics appeared, as in the previous successful run.\n\nExecuted names and durations:\n\n- testCaskNotificationCancelsPendingSearch — 17.077s\n- testCaskNotificationLeavesSearchForOutdatedDestination — 19.754s\n- testCaskNotificationLeavesSearchOnAlreadySelectedDestination — 23.817s\n- testFormulaeNotificationCancelsPendingSearch — 16.724s\n- testFormulaeNotificationLeavesSearchForOutdatedDestination — 19.587s\n- testFormulaeNotificationLeavesSearchOnAlreadySelectedDestination — 23.710s\n- testSearchFieldIsAvailable — 10.112s\n- testSearchingFindsCasksAndKeepsTheSidebarSelection — 23.166s\n\nThese test actual mock result arrival/removal, namespace-correct destinations, same-row notification refresh, pending debounce invalidation, nonzero search geometry/enabled state, and stable sidebar identity. Not a full suite/verification gate.\n\n## Actual visual and accessibility evidence\n\nLaunched exact temporary app bundles with `-BPMockBrew -BPMockWarmNotificationTarget casks -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier ''`. Original owned PIDs41636 and43751; fix42968. Used existing `beginMockNotificationSearch:` action after selecting All Casks row10 (enum checked); debounced mockvscode result actually rendered. No package install/upgrade/remove, real brew, installed app replacement, or global appearance/language change.\n\nInspected app-window-only screenshots:\n\n- Original `refactor-results-dark.png` is **Aqua despite its early filename**; it is the actual native system appearance this session. Correct dark evidence is `refactor-results-actual-dark.png`, visibly Dark Aqua. Original selected All Casks, readable mockvscode/name/status, native search/cancel control, spacing and mock badges intact. `refactor-results-aqua.png` additionally captures explicit Aqua.\n- Fix `fix-results-system.png` is Aqua; `fix-results-dark.png` is explicit Dark Aqua. Same search layout/content, no clipping/overlap or changed badge counts. Fix window was inactive during captures, so native dimmed chrome/inactive selection is expected; original screenshots also cover active window presentation.\n- Native AX dumps alongside screenshots show AXSearchField value mockvscode and327x38 geometry, selected stable `sidebar.casks.all`, and full sidebar descriptions with counts (formula installed3, outdated1, all4, leaves1, pinned1, repositories2; cask installed2/outdated1/all3). UI rows remain on cell text fields, no new AX identity changes. No VoiceOver speech or physical keyboard test claimed.\n- Appearance temporarily set via bounded LLDB `NSApp.appearance` to Aqua/DarkAqua and restored to original nil before each app quit. Actual `effectiveAppearance` recorded for Dark Aqua. No OS appearance preference mutation.\n- Initial debugger-only search expressions failed compilation due missing return-type knowledge for KVC; cast message return types as LLDB requested, then actual selector invocation succeeded. These were temporary diagnostic expressions, not product/test failures. All debuggers detached; no instrumentation entered source.\n\n## Coordination and exact state restoration\n\nInitial inspection found unrelated ControlPlane xcodebuild PID34993. It was left untouched; runtime launch held until it exited. Only isolated compilation/static review occurred concurrently. Display unlocked. First preliminary snapshot was not used for restoration; a **new snapshot in runtime-state/** was taken immediately before actual UI test/app launch.\n\nAfter every owned mock/runner/debugger exited, restored `com.scottdensmore.Cakebrew` persistent-domain envelope and the exact fresh cache bytes. Independent new Swift process reported `fresh-process preference dictionary equality: true; cache exact: true`. Cache backup SHA256 `01c1e93bc5bc2541d18a2d5711497c2290c13a0163d269d510bc2ae15a016df0`. Original app appearance nil restored for all owned mock lifetimes. Exact process-name inspection found no Cakebrew/xcodebuild/LLDB remaining; final command's exit1 was the expected final no-match pgrep, not restoration failure.\n\nEvidence/helper sources are isolated under this /private/tmp directory, nothing added to the repository. No user source/config changes touched. Source hashes checked unchanged after runtime release. Full verification and expert review remain separate gates.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788824784598,"completed_at_ms":1788824784598}}
