oval, namespace-correct destinations, same-row notification refresh, pending debounce invalidation, nonzero search geometry/enabled state, and stable sidebar identity. Not a full suite/verification gate.\\n\\n## Actual visual and accessibility evidence\\n\\nLaunched exact temporary app bundles with `-BPMockBrew -BPMockWarmNotificationTarget casks -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier ''`. Original owned PIDs41636 and43751; fix42968. Used existing `beginMockNotificationSearch:` action after selecting All Casks row10 (enum checked); debounced mockvscode result actually rendered. No package install/upgrade/remove, real brew, installed app replacement, or global appearance/language change.\\n\\nInspected app-window-only screenshots:\\n\\n- Original `refactor-results-dark.png` is **Aqua despite its early filename**; it is the actual native system appearance this session. Correct dark evidence is `refactor-results-actual-dark.png`, visibly Dark Aqua. Original selected All Casks, readable mockvscode/name/status, native search/cancel control, spacing and mock badges intact. `refactor-results-aqua.png` additionally captures explicit Aqua.\\n- Fix `fix-results-system.png` is Aqua; `fix-results-dark.png` is explicit Dark Aqua. Same search layout/content, no clipping/overlap or changed badge counts. Fix window was inactive during captures, so native dimmed chrome/inactive selection is expected; original screenshots also cover active window presentation.\\n- Native AX dumps alongside screenshots show AXSearchField value mockvscode and327x38 geometry, selected stable `sidebar.casks.all`, and full sidebar descriptions with counts (formula installed3, outdated1, all4, leaves1, pinned1, repositories2; cask installed2/outdated1/all3). UI rows remain on cell text fields, no new AX identity changes. No VoiceOver speech or physical keyboard test claimed.\\n- Appearance temporarily set via bounded LLDB `NSApp.appearance` to Aqua/DarkAqua and restored to original nil before each app quit. Actual `effectiveAppearance` recorded for Dark Aqua. No OS appearance preference mutation.\\n- Initial debugger-only search expressions failed compilation due missing return-type knowledge for KVC; cast message return types as LLDB requested, then actual selector invocation succeeded. These were temporary diagnostic expressions, not product/test failures. All debuggers detached; no instrumentation entered source.\\n\\n## Coordination and exact state restoration\\n\\nInitial inspection found unrelated ControlPlane xcodebuild PID34993. It was left untouched; runtime launch held until it exited. Only isolated compilation/static review occurred concurrently. Display unlocked. First preliminary snapshot was not used for restoration; a **new snapshot in runtime-state/** was taken immediately before actual UI test/app launch.\\n\\nAfter every owned mock/runner/debugger exited, restored `com.scottdensmore.Cakebrew` persistent-domain envelope and the exact fresh cache bytes. Independent new Swift process reported `fresh-process preference dictionary equality: true; cache exact: true`. Cache backup SHA256 `01c1e93bc5bc2541d18a2d5711497c2290c13a0163d269d510bc2ae15a016df0`. Original app appearance nil restored for all owned mock lifetimes. Exact process-name inspection found no Cakebrew/xcodebuild/LLDB remaining; final command's exit1 was the expected final no-match pgrep, not restoration failure.\\n\\nEvidence/helper sources are isolated under this /private/tmp directory, nothing added to the repository. No user source/config changes touched. Source hashes checked unchanged after runtime release. Full verification and expert review remain separate gates.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07e3a-7088-74f3-8263-cbdd479f00a0","create_time":1788824784.697486}}}
