hot was not published or copied.\n\n## Independent actual mock inspection\n\nPreflight showed unlocked display and no competing Cakebrew/xcodebuild/xctest process. Took a fresh preference/cache snapshot immediately before launch, not the implementer's prior snapshot. Launched the exact green binary from `/private/tmp/cakebrew-clear-search-journey.4MOdKu/DerivedData/Build/Products/Debug/Cakebrew.app` with `-BPMockBrew -BPMockWarmNotificationTarget casks -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier ''`; ownedPID68022.\n\nRead initial window-only screenshot/AX state and confirmed mockwget/mockgit loaded plus native menu accessibility title `Search Then Clear Mock Search` / selector identifier `clearMockSearchBeforeDebounce:`. Then invoked that existing mock action through bounded LLDB and detached, allowing the real main run loop/debounce to resume. After the debounce interval, captured `after-clear.png` and `after-clear-ax.txt` independently:\n\n- Empty native AXSearchField,327x38geometry.\n- Installed Formulae sidebar selected with stable identifier and3-item badge.\n- Actual mockwget1.0.0, pinned mockgit2.39.0, mockcurl8.0.0 rows; no mockvscode table row.\n- Native layout, row text, sidebar counts, pin glyph and footer readable, no clipping/overlap. Screenshot uses native system Aqua.\n\nUnchanged app layout and opposite-appearance behavior remain covered by this reviewer's earlier actual fix Aqua/DarkAqua screenshots and AX checks in `/private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/review.md`; only the mock-only menu/test adapter was added since. This pass made no appearance or host-setting change. No physical keyboard, VoiceOver speech, real brew, or full-suite run is claimed.\n\n## Restoration and release\n\nOwned app68022 quit normally; LLDB detached. Restored this pass's fresh `com.scottdensmore.Cakebrew` persistent-domain envelope/cache backup, then independently read in a new Swift process: `fresh-process preference dictionary equality: true; cache exact: true`. Exact process-name checks found no Cakebrew/LLDB. Final shell exit1 was final no-match pgrep, not a restoration error. Full source hash unchanged after release. Runtime/display/source lease released to root. Full verification/expert review still required separately.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4274},"formatted_output":"# Clear-search fix independent UI re-review — APPROVED\n\n2026-09-07. Read AGENTS.md and cakebrew-ui-review completely again; reviewed the updated full workspace inventory, incremental controller/UI-test/all-six-locales diff, source identity, and implementer red/green evidence. No source edits.\n\nWorktree `.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation`, base826371682a2044ea9cf8a95fdc4ac63804737b09. Full binary-diff-plus-sorted-untracked SHA256 before/after: `621fb48e01d4680b463be4076b5b6e0f6631a4cd0399c43c3829fb66fb46a2f6`.\n\n**UI gate approved; no actionable findings remain for the authorized queued-clear slice.** Previous missing journey finding is resolved. Separate completed-search/same-cask-row restoration observation remains pre-existing and outside this slice; nothing here claims it fixed.\n\n## Why coverage is adequate\n\nNew `testClearingQueuedSearchKeepsInstalledFormulaeVisible` observes initial installed mockwget and pinned mockgit, invokes the native mock menu, asserts empty search field, waits beyond the150ms debounce, checks stable `sidebar.formulae.installed`, verifies both installed rows remain, and checks no mockvscode result. It avoids keyboard/hittability assumptions and respects startup stabilization and stable sidebar identifiers.\n\nThe DEBUG/mock-only action `clearMockSearchBeforeDebounce:` mutates the actual toolbar field then invokes its actual delegate's `controlTextDidChange:` twice within one event, producing real toolbar submitSearch → controller performSearchWithString → coordinator scheduling/clearing. It does not fake coordinator state, replace rendering, or directly call the generation guard. The menu retains the existing DEBUG plus explicit BPMockBrew/warm-target gates; the one new English string is present in all six locales as required.\n\nIndependently read `/private/tmp/cakebrew-clear-search-journey.4MOdKu/red.log`: actual named test started, then failed at CakebrewUITests.m:1046 because mockwget disappeared,17.449s. This was the generation-increment-removal mutation, not a runner crash or unrelated failure. `green.log`: same named test passed16.708s,1test0failures, commandexit0. The1second inverted AX expectation itself did not catch that mutation, so it is not credited as the biting assertion; the following actual installed-row assertion did catch the stale result. This is adequate end-to-end regression evidence as a whole. No need to repeat mutation during independent UI review. The private failure screenshot was not published or copied.\n\n## Independent actual mock inspection\n\nPreflight showed unlocked display and no competing Cakebrew/xcodebuild/xctest process. Took a fresh preference/cache snapshot immediately before launch, not the implementer's prior snapshot. Launched the exact green binary from `/private/tmp/cakebrew-clear-search-journey.4MOdKu/DerivedData/Build/Products/Debug/Cakebrew.app` with `-BPMockBrew -BPMockWarmNotificationTarget casks -BPLastSelectedSidebarRow 1 -BPSortColumnIdentifier ''`; ownedPID68022.\n\nRead initial window-only screenshot/AX state and confirmed mockwget/mockgit loaded plus native menu accessibility title `Search Then Clear Mock Search` / selector identifier `clearMockSearchBeforeDebounce:`. Then invoked that existing mock action through bounded LLDB and detached, allowing the real main run loop/debounce to resume. After the debounce interval, captured `after-clear.png` and `after-clear-ax.txt` independently:\n\n- Empty native AXSearchField,327x38geometry.\n- Installed Formulae sidebar selected with stable identifier and3-item badge.\n- Actual mockwget1.0.0, pinned mockgit2.39.0, mockcurl8.0.0 rows; no mockvscode