ew/.worktrees/issue-152                 300e5f5 (detached HEAD)\n/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/issue-153                 1c29b7b (detached HEAD)\n/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/issue-157                 8549c80 (detached HEAD)\n/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation 8263716 [fix/search-clear-cancellation]\n/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/search-field-fix          2e6086b (detached HEAD)\n# Independent expert review decisions — 2026-09-07\n\nRead each worktree's complete AGENTS.md and cakebrew-code-review skill. Reviewed full branch against base 826371682a2044ea9cf8a95fdc4ac63804737b09 plus staged, unstaged, and every untracked file. Both indexes empty. No repository edits, app/test runtime launches, commits, or publication by reviewer. Full hashes independently recomputed. Hash input: git diff HEAD --binary followed by sorted untracked paths, each newline + path + newline + file bytes.\n\n## Original #143 behavior-preserving extraction: APPROVED\n\nWorktree: /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/issue-143-search\nFull hash: 724a7568797d88086da992df60a5faecd36bc5fa6184d78dc1b79b6a4bfd7e6b\n\nReviewed all six changed files: coordinator header/implementation/tests, controller wiring, Xcode project membership, and strengthened cask search journey. Traced toolbar submission, existing timer coalescing and main-queue dispatch, manager background filtering/main-queue publication, coordinator lifetime and navigation invalidation, raw sidebar restoration and controller rendering. No actionable regression. Existing queued-clear and completed same-row-clear limitations are preserved base behavior, not claimed fixed; separate search-clear worktree is excluded from this approval.\n\nPrerequisite evidence read: /private/tmp/cakebrew-143-verify.A7cxy6/handoff.md (warning-free Debug/Release, 442 unit tests with seven deliberate real-brew opt-in skips, UI target compilation, pristine 76/76 UI journeys); /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-ui-resume.l7XhKE/review.md (original UI gate approved); /private/tmp/cakebrew-143-implement.KJIxbP/handoff.md (observed absent-header red then six coordinator tests green). Sources released unchanged.\n\n## #142 localization report fresh rereview: APPROVED\n\nWorktree: /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/issue-142-l10n\nFull hash: e5abbc9b93c1fb33c2964d14a0c157286f40d1ca2c528adc7684326107aeb2a6\n\nPrior source c39d734d72e5298ba5ea7d4a7a4f2ccb8812d48d285475e63ef6a430ab743064 was NOT approved: P2 fixed live English-key and per-locale match counts in mandatory CI tests blocked ordinary valid additions/translations before the informational report. Read-only in-memory native-table probes confirmed successful reporter outputs of 255 vs hard-coded 254 keys and 126 vs hard-coded 127 German matches.\n\nFinding resolved at scripts/tests/localization-debt-tests.rb:180–228: real-input check now compares native current inventory, category-count consistency, exact disjoint English-key partition, and native missing/extra sets. Two deterministic fixture regressions cover valid additions to all six locales and translating an unreviewed German match. No fixed live debt thresholds or live metadata membership snapshots remain. Fixed fixture classification expectations and the narrow Formulae restoration regression are appropriate; malformed/duplicate input and invalid/stale metadata remain strict errors.\n\nRe-reviewed all ten changed files, including unchanged reporter/native decoding, classification metadata, safe deterministic Markdown/JSON output, CI ordering, AGENTS pointer, and five duplicate Formulae removals. No actionable findings remain; git diff --check clean. Source hash matches fresh verification, and sources released unchanged.\n\nPrerequisite evidence read: /private/tmp/cakebrew-l10n-review-fix.Yq8NGA/handoff.md (two observed old-policy failures then final 16 tests/364 assertions green); /private/tmp/cakebrew-142-reverify.igj5Km/handoff.md (fresh warning-free Debug/Release, 436 unit tests with seven deliberate opt-in skips, UI compilation, pristine 76/76 UI journeys without retry, reporter tests/native lints pass and exact state restoration); prior unchanged-surface UI approval /private/tmp/cakebrew-142-ui.Bwegyu/review.md.\n\nThese are pre-commit code-review gate approvals for the exact hashes only. Delivery authorization, subsequent integrations, and CI merge gates remain separate responsibilities.\n\n## Final queued-search-clear fix: APPROVED\n\nWorktree: /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/search-clear-cancellation\nFull hash: 621fb48e01d4680b463be4076b5b6e0f6631a4cd0399c43c3829fb66fb46a2f6\n\nRead this worktree's complete AGENTS.md and code-review skill, full base-8263716 diff, empty staged diff, and all twelve changed/untracked files. This includes the previously reviewed coordinator extraction and project membership, one generation increment at the start of endSearchReturningSidebarRow, two retained-callback unit regressions, the DEBUG/explicit-mock-only native queue-and-clear menu action, its new UI journey, and one matching English localization key in all six locales. Independently recomputed exact source hash; git diff --check clean. No source or runtime changes by reviewer.\n\nTraced actual field delegate controlTextDidChange -> toolbar submitSearch -> controller performSearchWithString -> coordinator queue/clear -> existing timer main-queue callback. Clear advances generation before manager cancellation, suppressing retained pre-clear callbacks without suppressing a new post-clear query. Weak coordinator lifetime, existing navigation invalidation, manager publication cancellation, and controller-owned row validation/rendering remain coherent. Mock adapter only submits actual field changes in one main event; it does not replace state, results, or sidebar behavior. Existing DEBUG plus BPMockBrew/warm-target gates keep the new action out of ordinary/release UI. All selector/title entries match.\n\nRead fresh prerequisites: /private/tmp/cakebrew-clear-final-verify.YTuRSJ/handoff.md (warning-free Debug/Release/UI compilation, 444 unit tests with seven deliberate opt-in skips, pristine 77/77 UI journeys without retries, new queued-clear test 12.699s, exact state restoration); /private/tmp/cakebrew-clear-ui-rereview.D0LyDg/review.md (UI gate approved); /private/tmp/cakebrew-search-clear-fix.fdjddj/handoff.md (two unit tests observed red, four intended assertions, then actual XCTest green); /private/tmp/cakebrew-clear-search-journey.4MOdKu/handoff.md (generation-removal mutation fails positive installed-row assertion, restoring guard passes same journey). The one-second inverted AX expectation did not itself catch the mutation and is not credited as the biting assertion. The later positive row assertion did, so the journey as a whole has observed regression sensitivity.\n\nNo actionable findings remain for this authorized queued-clear fix. The pre-existing completed-search/same-cask-row stale-table behavior is unchanged and outside scope, not claimed fixed. Existing duplicate Formulae keys are handled by the separate #142 slice and were not introduced here. Source released unchanged. This approval is only for the exact frozen full hash; later integration edits need the repository's fresh gates.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":" M .codex/config.toml\n?? workflow.md\n/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew                                      8263716 [main]\n/private/tmp/cakebrew-148-notification-navigation                                          cf41112 [feat/notification-navigation] prunable\n/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/ci-warning-cleanup        61857f4 (detached HEAD)\n/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.worktrees/issue-142-l10n   