{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:37:10.416Z","ordinal":22066,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-c3091816-f71e-44c4-a6e2-bd4148957095","query":"site:developers.openai.com codex custom agents config_file developer_instructions","action":{"type":"search","query":"site:developers.openai.com codex custom agents config_file developer_instructions","queries":null},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search0","snippet":"Developer-provided instructions that the model should follow, regardless of messages sent by the user. ... chat_completion_message_custom_tool_call: object { id, custom, type } ... Static predicted","title":"Chat | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/chat"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search1","snippet":"Codex Build and ship faster with our coding agent — everywhere you work. ... Discover what builders are creating with Codex and the OpenAI API,","title":"OpenAI Developers","url":"https://developers.openai.com/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search2","snippet":"Set `async: true` on a function or custom tool and return its result when ready using the original `call_id`. ... See Async tool calling for","title":"Model guidance | OpenAI API","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search3","snippet":"Provide text or image inputs to generate text or JSON outputs.Have the model call your own custom code or use built-in tools like web search","title":"Create a model response | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/responses/methods/create"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search4","snippet":"beta_custom_tool: object { name, type, allowed_callers, 4 more } ... Instructions given with the `developer` or `system` role take precedence over instructions given with the","title":"Responses | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/beta/subresources/responses"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search5","snippet":"GPT-5.3-Codex is optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5.3-Codex, refer to our","title":"GPT-5.3-Codex Model | OpenAI API","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.3-codex"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search6","snippet":"Just like GPT-5.1, the new GPT-5.2 has API features like custom tools, parameters to control verbosity and reasoning, and an allowed tools list. ... When","title":"Model guidance | OpenAI API","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model?model=gpt-5.2"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search7","snippet":"A version of GPT-5 optimized for agentic coding in Codex ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5-Codex, refer to our dedicated guide.","title":"GPT-5-Codex Model | OpenAI API","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5-codex"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search8","snippet":"instructions: string or array of ResponseInputItemA system (or developer) message inserted into the model’s context. ... * Built-in tools: Tools that are provided by OpenAI","title":"Get a model response | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/responses/methods/retrieve"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search9","snippet":"GPT-5.2-Codex is an upgraded version of GPT-5.2 optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. ... If you want to learn more about","title":"GPT-5.2-Codex Model | OpenAI API","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.2-codex"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search10","snippet":"GPT-6 Astra GPT-5.6 GPT-5.5 GPT-5.4 GPT-5.3 Codex GPT-5.2 GPT-5.1 GPT-5 GPT-4.1 ... import java.util.Map; ... instructions: \"Act as a coding agent. ... Find the exact","title":"Model guidance | OpenAI API","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model?model=gpt-4.1"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn28search11","snippet":"A custom tool that processes input using a specified format. ... A message input to the model with a role indicating instruction following hierarchy.Instructions given","title":"Responses | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/java/resources/beta/subresources/responses"}]},"started_at_ms":1788831429324,"completed_at_ms":1788831430415}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:37:10.619Z","ordinal":22067,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","session_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","root_turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","response_id":"resp_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f66c0658487d19e34f70d9760c654","usage":{"input_tokens":179800,"cached_input_tokens":172160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":171,"reasoning_output_tokens":28,"total_tokens":179971},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":352144,"cached_input_tokens":344064,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":377,"reasoning_output_tokens":28,"total_tokens":352521},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":297548239,"cached_input_tokens":293663872,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":541291,"reasoning_output_tokens":194248,"total_tokens":298089530}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:37:10.622Z","ordinal":22068,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a07ea9-77de-79f1-b6e3-3c3f0c7d242e","call_id":"call_wlQYhfS8u1Z7v1QF5SvWD1PU","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_get_users_recent_prs_in_repo\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nList the user's recent GitHub \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_search\",\"description\":\"Access repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nSearch GitHub files and return\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_list_sites\",\"description\":\"Use Sites to build, save, deploy, and inspect websites such as landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, portals, trackers,\"},{\"name\":\"web__run\",\"description\":\"Tools in the web namespace.\\n\\nTool for accessing the internet.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Examples of different commands available in this\"}]"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Chat | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/chat)\nciteturn28search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Developer-provided instructions that the model should follow, regardless of messages sent by the user. ... chat_completion_message_custom_tool_call: object { id, custom, type } ... Static predicted output content, such as the content of a text file that is being regenerated.\n\nDeveloper-provided instructions that the model should follow, regardless of messages sent by the user. With o1 models and newer, `developer` messages replace the previous `system` messages.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_function_call_option: object { name }\n\nSpecifying a particular function via `{\"name\": \"my_function\"}` forces the model to call that function.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_function_message_param: object { content, name, role }\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_function_tool: object { function, type }\n\nA function tool that can be used to generate a response.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_message: object { content, refusal, role, 4 more }\n\nA chat completion message generated by the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_message_custom_tool_call: object { id, custom, type }\n\nA call to a custom tool created by the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_message_function_tool_call: object { id, function, type }\n\nA call to a function tool created by the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_message_param: ChatCompletionDeveloperMessageParam { content, role, name } or ChatCompletionSystemMessageParam { content, role, name } or ChatCompletionUserMessageParam { content, role, name } or 3 more\n\nDeveloper-provided instructions that the model should follow, regardless of messages sent by the user. With o1 models and newer, `developer` messages replace the previous `system` messages.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_message_tool_call: ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall { id, function, type } or ChatCompletionMessageCustomToolCall { id, custom, type }\n\nA call to a function tool created by the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_modality: \"text\" or \"audio\"\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_named_tool_choice: object { function, type }\n\nSpecifies a tool the model should use. Use to force the model to call a specific function.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_named_tool_choice_custom: object { custom, type }\n\nSpecifies a tool the model should use. Use to force the model to call a specific custom tool.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_prediction_content: object { content, type }\n\nStatic predicted output content, such as the content of a text file that is being regenerated.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_role: \"developer\" or \"system\" or \"user\" or 3 more\n\nThe role of the author of a message\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_store_message: ChatCompletionMessage { content, refusal, role, 4 more }\n\nA chat completion message generated by the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_stream_options: object { include_obfuscation, include_usage }\n\nOptions for streaming response. Only set this when you set `stream: true`.\n\nView schema details\n\nchat_completion_system_message_param: object { content, role, name }\n\nDeveloper-provided instructions that the model should follow, regardless of messages sent by the user. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/)\nciteturn28search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Codex Build and ship faster with our coding agent — everywhere you work. ... Discover what builders are creating with Codex and the OpenAI API, and build your own version. ... Generate and edit images with stronger instruction following, flexible sizes, and high-fidelity image inputs. ... Help center Frequently asked account and billing questions Developer forum Discuss topics with other developers OpenAI Academy Courses and resources for learning about AI Status Check the status of OpenAI services\n\nImage: Illustration of polished OpenAI demo showcases\n\n## Featured\n\nImage\n\n## GPT Image 2 for image generation and editing\n\nGenerate and edit images with stronger instruction following, flexible sizes, and high-fidelity image inputs.\n\nRead the GPT Image 2 prompting guide\n\n### Codex for (almost) everything\n\nApril 16, 2026\n\nRealtime and audio Codex changelog Community page\n\n## Blog posts\n\nView all\n\nBuilding games with Astra How I built a procedural space exploration game in Codex, from concept art to planets you can land on. Sep 4, 2026 Codex Architectural visualization with Astra How I used Astra to design a house, refine its everyday details, and explore it through Blender camera tours and an Unreal Engine 5 walkthrough. Sep 4, 2026 Codex Automating repetitive work at OpenAI with Codex How Runme and WebMCP turn recurring engineering tasks into reviewable, reusable workflows. Aug 25, 2026 Codex\n\nHelp center Frequently asked account and billing questions Developer forum Discuss topics with other developers OpenAI Academy Courses and resources for learning about AI Status Check the status of OpenAI services\n\nAsk AI\n\n## Docs agent\n\nLoading docs agent...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModel guidance | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model)\nciteturn28search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Set `async: true` on a function or custom tool and return its result when ready using the original `call_id`. ... See Async tool calling for basic usage and a developer-defined wait-tool pattern. ... GPT-6 Astra also supports the existing API capabilities available with GPT-5.6, including computer use, Structured Outputs, streaming, Programmatic Tool Calling, multi-agent orchestration, prompt caching, persisted reasoning, compaction, and pro mode. ... It can be more sensitive to instructions contained in skills and other files, such as `AGENTS.md`. ...     `If a skill causes you to ask for permission or confirmation, pause, leave requested work unfinished, or diverge from the user's intent, name and link to the exact SKILL.md file you read, quote the relevant instruction, and briefly explain how it applies. ... Codex can apply the recommended changes in this guide with the OpenAI Docs skill. ... For Responses, remove `message.output_text.logprobs` from `include`.\n## Prompting best practices\n\nGPT-6 Astra is more intelligent and capable than prior models like GPT-5.6 Sol, and also exhibits behavior patterns that can be optimized through prompting the model for your use case.\n\n### GPT-6 Astra behavior\n\n  * Initiative and follow-through – The model is designed to be a more effective collaborator and is thus more likely to ask the user a question when additional input could materially change the result. This can cause it to stop when the user may expect it to make reasonable assumptions and persist.\n  * Instruction following – GPT-6 Astra is stronger at general instruction following than our previous models, giving you greater control over its behavior. It can be more sensitive to instructions contained in skills and other files, such as `AGENTS.md`. We strongly recommend auditing skills and other files accessible to your model for instructions that could influence its behavior.\n  * Personality and writing style – The model tends toward detailed, formatted responses and may use recurring phrases across sessions. Use this prompt to find silent and conflicting guidance when your application loads many skills and instruction files such as `AGENTS.md`.\n\n### Personality and writing style\n\nGPT-6 Astra tends to use lists, tables and Markdown to make responses scannable. If your application needs prose with less formatting, specify that preference.\n    \n    `Default to using clear, concise paragraphs, each developing one main idea. Use lists only when the information is genuinely parallel, sequential, or easier to compare, and avoid nested lists unless the hierarchy cannot be expressed clearly in prose. Use plain, simple language: familiar words, concrete examples, and precise verbs. Prefer active voice and direct statements.\n    \n    Make sure to state the main point clearly and early, then develop it with the explanation and detail the reader needs. Let each sentence build on what came before. Develop the points that matter and provide enough support to be useful.`\n\nFor technical communication, the following prompt helps strike a balance between using clear, coherent language while remaining domain appropriate:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate a model response | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/responses/methods/create)\nciteturn28search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Provide text or image inputs to generate text or JSON outputs.Have the model call your own custom code or use built-in tools like web search or file search to use your own data as input for the model’s response. ... --instructions: optional stringA system (or developer) message inserted into the model’s context.\n--instructions: optional string\n\nA system (or developer) message inserted into the model’s context.\n\nWhen using along with `previous_response_id`, the instructions from a previous response will not be carried over to the next response. This makes it simple to swap out system (or developer) messages in new responses.\n\n--max-output-tokens: optional number\n\nAn upper bound for the number of tokens that can be generated for a response, including visible output tokens and reasoning tokens.\n\n--max-tool-calls: optional number\n\nThe maximum number of total calls to built-in tools that can be processed in a response. This maximum number applies across all built-in tool calls, not per individual tool. Any further attempts to call a tool by the model will be ignored.\n\n--metadata: optional map[string]\n\nSet of 16 key-value pairs that can be attached to an object. This can be useful for storing additional information about the object in a structured format, and querying for objects via API or the dashboard.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResponses | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/beta/subresources/responses)\nciteturn28search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; beta_custom_tool: object { name, type, allowed_callers, 4 more } ... Instructions given with the `developer` or `system` role take precedence over instructions given with the `user` role. ... A tool call that applies file diffs by creating, deleting, or updating files. ... beta_response_content: BetaResponseInputText { text, type, prompt_cache_breakpoint } or BetaResponseInputImage { detail, type, file_id, 2 more } or BetaResponseInputFile { type, detail, file_data, 4 more } or 3 more ... beta_response_input_item: BetaEasyInputMessage { content, role, phase, type } or object { content, role, agent, 2 more } or BetaResponseOutputMessage { id, content, role, 4 more } or 33 more\nA message input to the model with a role indicating instruction following hierarchy. Instructions given with the `developer` or `system` role take precedence over instructions given with the `user` role. Messages with the `assistant` role are presumed to have been generated by the model in previous interactions.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_file_search_tool: object { type, vector_store_ids, filters, 2 more }\n\nA tool that searches for relevant content from uploaded files. Learn more about the file search tool.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_function_shell_tool: object { type, allowed_callers, environment }\n\nA tool that allows the model to execute shell commands.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_function_tool: object { name, parameters, strict, 6 more }\n\nDefines a function in your own code the model can choose to call. Learn more about function calling.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_inline_skill: object { description, name, source, type }\n\nbeta_response_input_audio: object { input_audio, type }\n\nAn audio input to the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_response_input_content: BetaResponseInputText { text, type, prompt_cache_breakpoint } or BetaResponseInputImage { detail, type, file_id, 2 more } or BetaResponseInputFile { type, detail, file_data, 4 more }\n\nA text input to the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_response_input_file: object { type, detail, file_data, 4 more }\n\nA file input to the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_response_input_file_content: object { type, detail, file_data, 4 more }\n\nA file input to the model.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_response_input_image: object { detail, type, file_id, 2 more }\n\nAn image input to the model. Learn about image inputs.\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_response_input_image_content: object { type, detail, file_id, 2 more }\n\nAn image input to the model. Learn about image inputs\n\nView schema details\n\nbeta_response_input_item: BetaEasyInputMessage { content, role, phase, type } or object { content, role, agent, 2 more } or BetaResponseOutputMessage { id, content, role, 4 more } or 33 more\n\nA message input to the model with a role indicating instruction following hierarchy. Instructions given with the `developer` or `system` role take precedence over instructions given with the `user` role. Messages with the `assistant` role are presumed to have been generated by the model in previous interactions.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGPT-5.3-Codex Model | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.3-codex)\nciteturn28search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; GPT-5.3-Codex is optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5.3-Codex, refer to our dedicated guide. ... Text tokens\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModel guidance | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model?model=gpt-5.2)\nciteturn28search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Just like GPT-5.1, the new GPT-5.2 has API features like custom tools, parameters to control verbosity and reasoning, and an allowed tools list. ... When the GPT-5 model family launched, we introduced a new capability called custom tools, which lets models send any raw text as tool call input but still constrain outputs if desired. ... The model can send any raw text—code, SQL queries, shell commands, configuration files, or long-form prose—directly to your tool. ... To enable preambles, add a system or developer instruction—for example: “Before you call a tool, explain why you are calling it.” ... GPT-5.2-Codex prompting guide ... ## Docs agent\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGPT-5-Codex Model | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5-codex)\nciteturn28search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; A version of GPT-5 optimized for agentic coding in Codex ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5-Codex, refer to our dedicated guide. ... Text tokens\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGet a model response | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/responses/methods/retrieve)\nciteturn28search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; instructions: string or array of ResponseInputItemA system (or developer) message inserted into the model’s context. ...   * Built-in tools: Tools that are provided by OpenAI that extend the model’s capabilities, like web search or file search. ...   * Function calls (custom tools): Functions that are defined by you, enabling the model to call your own code with strongly typed arguments and outputs.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGPT-5.2-Codex Model | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.2-codex)\nciteturn28search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; GPT-5.2-Codex is an upgraded version of GPT-5.2 optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. ... If you want to learn more about prompting GPT-5.2-Codex, refer to our dedicated guide. ... Text tokens\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModel guidance | OpenAI API (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model?model=gpt-4.1)\nciteturn28search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; GPT-6 Astra GPT-5.6 GPT-5.5 GPT-5.4 GPT-5.3 Codex GPT-5.2 GPT-5.1 GPT-5 GPT-4.1 ...     import java.util.Map; ...       instructions: \"Act as a coding agent. ... Find the exact error message text (e.g. ...     70 APPLY_PATCH_TOOL_DESC = \"\"\"This is a custom utility that makes it more convenient to add, remove, move, or edit code files. `apply_patch` effectively allows you to execute a diff/patch against a file, but the format of the diff specification is unique to this task, so pay careful attention to these instructions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResponses | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/java/resources/beta/subresources/responses)\nciteturn28search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; A custom tool that processes input using a specified format. ... A message input to the model with a role indicating instruction following hierarchy.Instructions given with the `developer` or `system` role take precedence over instructions given with the `user` role. ... A text input to the model. ... class BetaResponseInputFile:\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","create_time":1788831430.622391}}}
