{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:56.819Z","ordinal":22136,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f680672f887d1aa1599201d18ccbd","status":"completed","call_id":"call_tNq6WFx7JKBs5rooyHBQpPQ5","name":"exec","input":"const roles = [\n[\"plan\",\"Plan a Cakebrew change or spike when requirements, framework behavior, architectural tradeoffs or vertical-slice scope need resolution.\",\"Planning\",\"Discovery and scoping\",\"Read the assigned problem and trace the relevant code and tests. Return the planner handoff specified in AGENTS.md, distinguishing observations from assumptions and identifying what must be measured. Keep any authorized spike isolated and account for its cleanup; do not implement production changes.\"],\n[\"implement\",\"Implement one scoped Cakebrew feature, bugfix or behavior-changing refactor under red-green-refactor TDD, including fixes returned by quality gates.\",\"Implementation\",\"Implementation\",\"Use the assigned acceptance criteria and file ownership. Return the implementer handoff specified in AGENTS.md, including actual expected-failure evidence and the resulting diff. Flag missing scope before expanding it. Leave gate decisions and delivery to their assigned roles.\"],\n[\"ui-review\",\"Independently review a stabilized user-visible Cakebrew change for AppKit layout, appearance, accessibility and UI journey coverage.\",\"UI Review\",\"Quality gates\",\"Inspect the supplied diff and run the UI review defined in AGENTS.md using its testing contracts and environment diagnostics. Return observed evidence and a clear approval, actionable findings or blocker. Do not repair the implementation or mistake unavailable visual coverage for a pass.\"],\n[\"verify\",\"Validate a stabilized Cakebrew slice with the complete applicable verification gate and source-matched evidence, without editing source.\",\"Verification\",\"Quality gates\",\"Run the applicable verification gate using AGENTS.md commands and testing contracts. Return commands, source identity, diagnostics, executed counts/skips and evidence paths. Distinguish product failures from environment blockers. Report pass, fail or blocked without fixing sources or waiving checks.\"],\n[\"code-review\",\"Independently review a verified Cakebrew branch and all uncommitted files before commit, or re-review after fixes invalidate approval.\",\"Expert Code Review\",\"Quality gates\",\"Require current verification evidence, then inspect the full review scope defined in AGENTS.md. Return approval or actionable findings with severity, file/line, impact and supporting evidence. Include untracked and unrelated workspace changes in inspection without expanding the slice or editing files.\"],\n[\"workflow\",\"Orchestrate a Cakebrew feature, bugfix or behavior-changing refactor across planning, implementation, independent quality gates and authorized delivery.\",\"Workflow\",\"Role orchestration and evidence\",\"Dispatch the configured roles in AGENTS.md lifecycle order with its assignment and handoff contracts. Keep requirements, cross-role decisions and delivery with the primary agent. Route findings through its fix loop and track which evidence is current; use its concurrency rules before overlapping work.\"],\n[\"deliver\",\"Deliver a verified Cakebrew slice when the user authorizes committing, publishing, opening a PR or merging; coordinate any required remediation through the workflow.\",\"Delivery\",\"Delivery\",\"Apply only the authorized delivery stages in AGENTS.md. Check source-matched gate evidence before mutation, and use its CI, assigned-review, stacked-PR and cleanup rules. Route stale evidence or in-scope findings back through $cakebrew-workflow; hold the affected delivery stage. Report genuine authority or environment blockers without silently bypassing gates.\"]\n];\nconst entries=[];\nfor(const [suffix,desc,title,section,body] of roles){\nentries.push([`.agents/skills/cakebrew-${suffix}/SKILL.md`,`---\\nname: cakebrew-${suffix}\\ndescription: ${desc}\\n---\\n\\n# Cakebrew ${title}\\n\\nRead the repository's \\`AGENTS.md\\` completely before acting. It is the sole\\nproject authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **${section}**\\nsection and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\\n\\n${body}\\n`]);\n}\nconst agents=[\n[\"planner\",\"plan\",\"Discovery and planning for one Cakebrew slice; measures unknowns and returns an implementation handoff.\",\"workspace-write\",\"Work from the assigned problem and repository evidence. Own only the explicitly assigned planning/spike artifacts. Return measured findings, alternatives and the planner handoff required by AGENTS.md; identify assumptions and cleanup. Do not implement production changes.\"],\n[\"implementer\",\"implement\",\"Implementation of one explicitly owned Cakebrew slice with observed TDD evidence; no self-approval or delivery.\",\"workspace-write\",\"Confirm the assigned worktree, acceptance criteria and file ownership. You are not alone in the codebase: preserve other agents' and the user's changes. Return the implementer handoff required by AGENTS.md, including expected-failure and passing-test evidence. Return findings to the primary agent instead of approving your own work.\"],\n[\"ui-reviewer\",\"ui-review\",\"Independent AppKit visual, accessibility and journey review of a stable Cakebrew diff.\",\"workspace-write\",\"Review the assigned stable diff using the UI gate and testing contracts in AGENTS.md. You may run builds and authorized mock UI checks but may not edit sources. Return the UI reviewer handoff with observed evidence and approval, actionable findings or an environment blocker.\"],\n[\"verifier\",\"verify\",\"Independent source-matched Cakebrew build, test and diagnostic verification; reports failures without fixing them.\",\"workspace-write\",\"Validate the assigned stable state using the applicable verification gate in AGENTS.md. You may generate build and test artifacts, but may not edit sources. Return the verifier handoff with actual execution evidence and pass, fail or blocked status. A runner failure or missing execution is not a passing product test.\"],\n[\"code-reviewer\",\"code-review\",\"Independent pre-commit review of the full verified Cakebrew branch and workspace diff; read-only findings or approval.\",\"read-only\",\"Inspect the full assigned branch and workspace diff after confirming current verification evidence. Apply the expert review gate in AGENTS.md and return its code-reviewer handoff. Stay read-only; report actionable findings or approval, never silently fix or waive a finding.\"]\n];\nfor(const [name,skill,desc,sandbox,instructions] of agents){\nentries.push([`.codex/agents/cakebrew-${name}.toml`,`name = \"cakebrew-${name}\"\\ndescription = \"${desc}\"\\nsandbox_mode = \"${sandbox}\"\\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\\nRead AGENTS.md completely before acting. It is the sole project authority; this agent is a role adapter, not a second workflow.\\nInvoke $cakebrew-${skill}. Follow the assignment, evidence and concurrency contracts in AGENTS.md.\\n${instructions}\\nKeep the assignment bounded. Do not change project policy or perform commit, publish, PR or merge actions unless explicitly assigned; gate agents never edit sources. Report missing inputs or authority to the primary agent.\\n\"\"\"\\n`]);\n}\nentries.push([\"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\"# Contributing\\n\\nRead [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the authoritative workflow, build and test\\ncommands, conventions and architecture decisions for Cakebrew.\\n\\nUse the repository's issue templates to report bugs or propose improvements.\\nReport security concerns through [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), not a public issue.\\n\"]);\nlet patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n\";\nfor(const [path,body] of entries){\nconst old=await tools.exec_command({cmd:`cat ${path}`,max_output_tokens:5000});\nif(old.exit_code!==0)throw Error(path);\npatch+=\"*** Update File: /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/\"+path+\"\\n@@\\n\"+old.output.trimEnd().split(\"\\n\").map(x=>\"-\"+x).join(\"\\n\")+\"\\n\"+body.trimEnd().split(\"\\n\").map(x=>\"+\"+x).join(\"\\n\")+\"\\n\";\n}\npatch+=\"*** End Patch\";\nstore(\"adapters_patch\",patch);\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","create_time":1788831746.925741}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:56.886Z","ordinal":22137,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","session_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","root_turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","response_id":"resp_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f6802a6c087d1ba65be5f9ff54936","usage":{"input_tokens":65669,"cached_input_tokens":60800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1674,"reasoning_output_tokens":90,"total_tokens":67343},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1469192,"cached_input_tokens":1386368,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18292,"reasoning_output_tokens":1006,"total_tokens":1487484},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":298665287,"cached_input_tokens":294706176,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":559206,"reasoning_output_tokens":195226,"total_tokens":299224493}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:56.957Z","ordinal":22138,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-309a104d-f264-46d0-9507-fa280eacd820","process_id":"13080","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-plan/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-plan/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/cakebrew-plan/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: cakebrew-plan\ndescription: Plan or spike a Cakebrew change before implementation when requirements, architecture, framework behavior, integration boundaries, or vertical-slice scope need to be resolved.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Plan\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Stay in the planner role: do not implement\nproduction code.\n\n- Inspect the repository and trace the relevant execution paths.\n- Identify unknowns that require measurement. Use the smallest disposable\n  spike needed, keep it out of production paths, and remove it before returning.\n- Compare viable alternatives by architectural fit, complexity, performance\n  and maintenance burden.\n- Define the smallest cohesive vertical slice, its acceptance criteria, test\n  seams and expected red test.\n- Report assumptions, evidence, risks, rejected alternatives and an ordered\n  slice plan. Clearly distinguish measured behavior from inference.\n\nPreserve all unrelated changes. Do not commit, push, open a PR or change\nproject instructions.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-plan\ndescription: Plan or spike a Cakebrew change before implementation when requirements, architecture, framework behavior, integration boundaries, or vertical-slice scope need to be resolved.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Plan\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Stay in the planner role: do not implement\nproduction code.\n\n- Inspect the repository and trace the relevant execution paths.\n- Identify unknowns that require measurement. Use the smallest disposable\n  spike needed, keep it out of production paths, and remove it before returning.\n- Compare viable alternatives by architectural fit, complexity, performance\n  and maintenance burden.\n- Define the smallest cohesive vertical slice, its acceptance criteria, test\n  seams and expected red test.\n- Report assumptions, evidence, risks, rejected alternatives and an ordered\n  slice plan. Clearly distinguish measured behavior from inference.\n\nPreserve all unrelated changes. Do not commit, push, open a PR or change\nproject instructions.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4477},"formatted_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-plan\ndescription: Plan or spike a Cakebrew change before implementation when requirements, architecture, framework behavior, integration boundaries, or vertical-slice scope need to be resolved.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Plan\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Stay in the planner role: do not implement\nproduction code.\n\n- Inspect the repository and trace the relevant execution paths.\n- Identify unknowns that require measurement. Use the smallest disposable\n  spike needed, keep it out of production paths, and remove it before returning.\n- Compare viable alternatives by architectural fit, complexity, performance\n  and maintenance burden.\n- Define the smallest cohesive vertical slice, its acceptance criteria, test\n  seams and expected red test.\n- Report assumptions, evidence, risks, rejected alternatives and an ordered\n  slice plan. Clearly distinguish measured behavior from inference.\n\nPreserve all unrelated changes. Do not commit, push, open a PR or change\nproject instructions.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831776957,"completed_at_ms":1788831776957}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:57.593Z","ordinal":22139,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a29fb565-ca0e-4291-8ba0-cf83f9192611","process_id":"58325","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-implement/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-implement/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/cakebrew-implement/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: cakebrew-implement\ndescription: Implement an assigned Cakebrew vertical slice under strict red-green-refactor TDD after its scope and acceptance criteria are established.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Implement\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely and accept explicit ownership of the assigned files\nor behavior. Other work may exist in the checkout; never revert or absorb it.\n\n1. Confirm the slice, acceptance criteria and intended test seam.\n2. Add the smallest focused test first and run it to observe the expected red.\n3. Implement only enough production code to make it green.\n4. Refactor with the focused test and relevant fast suite green.\n5. Inspect all staged, unstaged and untracked files and remove scratch or debug\n   artifacts created by this implementation.\n\nIf red was not observed, perform and report the mutation proof required by\n`AGENTS.md`. Stop after implementation evidence; do not self-approve the UI,\nverification or expert-review gates. Never commit or publish; delivery belongs\nto the primary agent under `$cakebrew-deliver`.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-implement\ndescription: Implement an assigned Cakebrew vertical slice under strict red-green-refactor TDD after its scope and acceptance criteria are established.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Implement\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely and accept explicit ownership of the assigned files\nor behavior. Other work may exist in the checkout; never revert or absorb it.\n\n1. Confirm the slice, acceptance criteria and intended test seam.\n2. Add the smallest focused test first and run it to observe the expected red.\n3. Implement only enough production code to make it green.\n4. Refactor with the focused test and relevant fast suite green.\n5. Inspect all staged, unstaged and untracked files and remove scratch or debug\n   artifacts created by this implementation.\n\nIf red was not observed, perform and report the mutation proof required by\n`AGENTS.md`. Stop after implementation evidence; do not self-approve the UI,\nverification or expert-review gates. Never commit or publish; delivery belongs\nto the primary agent under `$cakebrew-deliver`.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6835},"formatted_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-implement\ndescription: Implement an assigned Cakebrew vertical slice under strict red-green-refactor TDD after its scope and acceptance criteria are established.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Implement\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely and accept explicit ownership of the assigned files\nor behavior. Other work may exist in the checkout; never revert or absorb it.\n\n1. Confirm the slice, acceptance criteria and intended test seam.\n2. Add the smallest focused test first and run it to observe the expected red.\n3. Implement only enough production code to make it green.\n4. Refactor with the focused test and relevant fast suite green.\n5. Inspect all staged, unstaged and untracked files and remove scratch or debug\n   artifacts created by this implementation.\n\nIf red was not observed, perform and report the mutation proof required by\n`AGENTS.md`. Stop after implementation evidence; do not self-approve the UI,\nverification or expert-review gates. Never commit or publish; delivery belongs\nto the primary agent under `$cakebrew-deliver`.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831777592,"completed_at_ms":1788831777593}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:57.874Z","ordinal":22140,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-707c1290-2c9b-4003-9aef-f731948733aa","process_id":"8235","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-ui-review/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-ui-review/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/cakebrew-ui-review/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: cakebrew-ui-review\ndescription: Review a user-visible Cakebrew change for AppKit conventions, layout, appearance, accessibility, and UI journey coverage after implementation stabilizes.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Ui Review\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the changed surface independently; do not\nedit source files.\n\n- Inspect the branch and workspace diff to identify affected journeys.\n- Launch against `-BPMockBrew` and verify the relevant state visually.\n- Check layout, dark mode, badges, accessibility identity and macOS idioms.\n- Prefer an existing or proposed `CakebrewUITests` assertion for behavior that\n  should not depend on visual judgment.\n- Account for the documented locked-screen and headless-CI limitations before\n  classifying a failure.\n\nReturn prioritized, reproducible findings with file or UI location and expected\nbehavior. Say explicitly when the gate passes. Send fixes back to the\nimplementer rather than making them in the review pass.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-ui-review\ndescription: Review a user-visible Cakebrew change for AppKit conventions, layout, appearance, accessibility, and UI journey coverage after implementation stabilizes.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Ui Review\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the changed surface independently; do not\nedit source files.\n\n- Inspect the branch and workspace diff to identify affected journeys.\n- Launch against `-BPMockBrew` and verify the relevant state visually.\n- Check layout, dark mode, badges, accessibility identity and macOS idioms.\n- Prefer an existing or proposed `CakebrewUITests` assertion for behavior that\n  should not depend on visual judgment.\n- Account for the documented locked-screen and headless-CI limitations before\n  classifying a failure.\n\nReturn prioritized, reproducible findings with file or UI location and expected\nbehavior. Say explicitly when the gate passes. Send fixes back to the\nimplementer rather than making them in the review pass.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6329},"formatted_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-ui-review\ndescription: Review a user-visible Cakebrew change for AppKit conventions, layout, appearance, accessibility, and UI journey coverage after implementation stabilizes.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Ui Review\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the changed surface independently; do not\nedit source files.\n\n- Inspect the branch and workspace diff to identify affected journeys.\n- Launch against `-BPMockBrew` and verify the relevant state visually.\n- Check layout, dark mode, badges, accessibility identity and macOS idioms.\n- Prefer an existing or proposed `CakebrewUITests` assertion for behavior that\n  should not depend on visual judgment.\n- Account for the documented locked-screen and headless-CI limitations before\n  classifying a failure.\n\nReturn prioritized, reproducible findings with file or UI location and expected\nbehavior. Say explicitly when the gate passes. Send fixes back to the\nimplementer rather than making them in the review pass.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831777874,"completed_at_ms":1788831777874}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:58.183Z","ordinal":22141,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f550bcd4-cbce-4205-97f1-dd8e2d749f22","process_id":"80483","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-verify/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-verify/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/cakebrew-verify/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: cakebrew-verify\ndescription: Run Cakebrew's complete local verification gate after implementation or fixes, including required builds, tests, warnings checks, and UI-target coverage.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Verify\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely and use its current commands as the authority. Do\nnot edit source files.\n\nRun the gate from the beginning in its documented order:\n\n1. Debug build, warning-free.\n2. Release build, warning-free.\n3. Full unit suite.\n4. UI test target compilation.\n5. UI journeys before PR creation, subject to the documented display checks.\n\nValidate that each instrument actually exercised the intended target; do not\ntreat an exit code or silent output alone as proof. Separate genuine product or\nsetup failures from sandbox, signing, locked-screen or headless-environment\nartifacts. Return a compact command-by-command result with decisive diagnostics\nand an explicit pass/fail. Route failures to the implementer.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-verify\ndescription: Run Cakebrew's complete local verification gate after implementation or fixes, including required builds, tests, warnings checks, and UI-target coverage.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Verify\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely and use its current commands as the authority. Do\nnot edit source files.\n\nRun the gate from the beginning in its documented order:\n\n1. Debug build, warning-free.\n2. Release build, warning-free.\n3. Full unit suite.\n4. UI test target compilation.\n5. UI journeys before PR creation, subject to the documented display checks.\n\nValidate that each instrument actually exercised the intended target; do not\ntreat an exit code or silent output alone as proof. Separate genuine product or\nsetup failures from sandbox, signing, locked-screen or headless-environment\nartifacts. Return a compact command-by-command result with decisive diagnostics\nand an explicit pass/fail. Route failures to the implementer.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5427},"formatted_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-verify\ndescription: Run Cakebrew's complete local verification gate after implementation or fixes, including required builds, tests, warnings checks, and UI-target coverage.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Verify\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely and use its current commands as the authority. Do\nnot edit source files.\n\nRun the gate from the beginning in its documented order:\n\n1. Debug build, warning-free.\n2. Release build, warning-free.\n3. Full unit suite.\n4. UI test target compilation.\n5. UI journeys before PR creation, subject to the documented display checks.\n\nValidate that each instrument actually exercised the intended target; do not\ntreat an exit code or silent output alone as proof. Separate genuine product or\nsetup failures from sandbox, signing, locked-screen or headless-environment\nartifacts. Return a compact command-by-command result with decisive diagnostics\nand an explicit pass/fail. Route failures to the implementer.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831778182,"completed_at_ms":1788831778183}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:58.453Z","ordinal":22142,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c185fdfb-8a6b-40c8-ae36-25cf021dc025","process_id":"5076","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-code-review/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-code-review/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/cakebrew-code-review/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: cakebrew-code-review\ndescription: Perform the independent pre-commit expert review of a Cakebrew branch and all uncommitted files after verification passes.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Code Review\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the full branch diff against its base plus\nall staged, unstaged and untracked files. Do not edit source files.\n\nPrioritize correctness, regressions, Objective-C and AppKit idioms, memory and\nconcurrency safety, performance, architecture, edge cases, mock fidelity and\nmissing tests. Trace the actual execution path before reporting a problem.\nAvoid style-only comments unless they reveal a concrete maintenance or defect\nrisk.\n\nReturn findings ordered by severity with precise file and line references,\nimpact and a reproducible rationale. If there are no actionable findings, say\nthe gate is approved. Any fix belongs to the implementer and invalidates the\nprior verification result.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-code-review\ndescription: Perform the independent pre-commit expert review of a Cakebrew branch and all uncommitted files after verification passes.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Code Review\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the full branch diff against its base plus\nall staged, unstaged and untracked files. Do not edit source files.\n\nPrioritize correctness, regressions, Objective-C and AppKit idioms, memory and\nconcurrency safety, performance, architecture, edge cases, mock fidelity and\nmissing tests. Trace the actual execution path before reporting a problem.\nAvoid style-only comments unless they reveal a concrete maintenance or defect\nrisk.\n\nReturn findings ordered by severity with precise file and line references,\nimpact and a reproducible rationale. If there are no actionable findings, say\nthe gate is approved. Any fix belongs to the implementer and invalidates the\nprior verification result.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6140},"formatted_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-code-review\ndescription: Perform the independent pre-commit expert review of a Cakebrew branch and all uncommitted files after verification passes.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Code Review\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the full branch diff against its base plus\nall staged, unstaged and untracked files. Do not edit source files.\n\nPrioritize correctness, regressions, Objective-C and AppKit idioms, memory and\nconcurrency safety, performance, architecture, edge cases, mock fidelity and\nmissing tests. Trace the actual execution path before reporting a problem.\nAvoid style-only comments unless they reveal a concrete maintenance or defect\nrisk.\n\nReturn findings ordered by severity with precise file and line references,\nimpact and a reproducible rationale. If there are no actionable findings, say\nthe gate is approved. Any fix belongs to the implementer and invalidates the\nprior verification result.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831778452,"completed_at_ms":1788831778453}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:58.707Z","ordinal":22143,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-51603737-72eb-4f1e-a8c6-fe1e42eb203e","process_id":"24187","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: cakebrew-workflow\ndescription: Orchestrate a complete Cakebrew feature, bugfix, or behavior-changing refactor through planning, TDD implementation, UI review when applicable, verification, expert review, and delivery gates.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Workflow\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole authority for the\nworkflow, commands, architecture and delivery rules; this skill only routes the\nwork through the configured roles.\n\n1. Use `cakebrew-planner` with `$cakebrew-plan` to validate assumptions and\n   define the smallest vertical slice. Any spike is disposable.\n2. Inspect repository state, synchronize the latest `main`, preserve unrelated\n   changes, and create the required branch before production edits.\n3. Give `cakebrew-implementer` explicit ownership of the slice and invoke\n   `$cakebrew-implement`. Require observed red-green-refactor evidence.\n4. If a user-visible surface changed, run `cakebrew-ui-reviewer` with\n   `$cakebrew-ui-review` after implementation is stable.\n5. Run `cakebrew-verifier` with `$cakebrew-verify`, then\n   `cakebrew-code-reviewer` with `$cakebrew-code-review`.\n6. Route every actionable finding back to the implementer. After any source\n   edit, repeat verification and expert review; repeat UI review too when the\n   fix changes the visible surface.\n7. Keep delivery with the primary agent. Invoke `$cakebrew-deliver` only when\n   the user has authorized the relevant commit, push, PR or merge action.\n\nDo not run a mutating agent concurrently with a verifier or reviewer against\nthe same worktree. Use isolated worktrees when independent passes truly need to\nrun in parallel. Return concise role summaries and evidence to the primary\nagent instead of raw logs.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-workflow\ndescription: Orchestrate a complete Cakebrew feature, bugfix, or behavior-changing refactor through planning, TDD implementation, UI review when applicable, verification, expert review, and delivery gates.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Workflow\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole authority for the\nworkflow, commands, architecture and delivery rules; this skill only routes the\nwork through the configured roles.\n\n1. Use `cakebrew-planner` with `$cakebrew-plan` to validate assumptions and\n   define the smallest vertical slice. Any spike is disposable.\n2. Inspect repository state, synchronize the latest `main`, preserve unrelated\n   changes, and create the required branch before production edits.\n3. Give `cakebrew-implementer` explicit ownership of the slice and invoke\n   `$cakebrew-implement`. Require observed red-green-refactor evidence.\n4. If a user-visible surface changed, run `cakebrew-ui-reviewer` with\n   `$cakebrew-ui-review` after implementation is stable.\n5. Run `cakebrew-verifier` with `$cakebrew-verify`, then\n   `cakebrew-code-reviewer` with `$cakebrew-code-review`.\n6. Route every actionable finding back to the implementer. After any source\n   edit, repeat verification and expert review; repeat UI review too when the\n   fix changes the visible surface.\n7. Keep delivery with the primary agent. Invoke `$cakebrew-deliver` only when\n   the user has authorized the relevant commit, push, PR or merge action.\n\nDo not run a mutating agent concurrently with a verifier or reviewer against\nthe same worktree. Use isolated worktrees when independent passes truly need to\nrun in parallel. Return concise role summaries and evidence to the primary\nagent instead of raw logs.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5885},"formatted_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-workflow\ndescription: Orchestrate a complete Cakebrew feature, bugfix, or behavior-changing refactor through planning, TDD implementation, UI review when applicable, verification, expert review, and delivery gates.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Workflow\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole authority for the\nworkflow, commands, architecture and delivery rules; this skill only routes the\nwork through the configured roles.\n\n1. Use `cakebrew-planner` with `$cakebrew-plan` to validate assumptions and\n   define the smallest vertical slice. Any spike is disposable.\n2. Inspect repository state, synchronize the latest `main`, preserve unrelated\n   changes, and create the required branch before production edits.\n3. Give `cakebrew-implementer` explicit ownership of the slice and invoke\n   `$cakebrew-implement`. Require observed red-green-refactor evidence.\n4. If a user-visible surface changed, run `cakebrew-ui-reviewer` with\n   `$cakebrew-ui-review` after implementation is stable.\n5. Run `cakebrew-verifier` with `$cakebrew-verify`, then\n   `cakebrew-code-reviewer` with `$cakebrew-code-review`.\n6. Route every actionable finding back to the implementer. After any source\n   edit, repeat verification and expert review; repeat UI review too when the\n   fix changes the visible surface.\n7. Keep delivery with the primary agent. Invoke `$cakebrew-deliver` only when\n   the user has authorized the relevant commit, push, PR or merge action.\n\nDo not run a mutating agent concurrently with a verifier or reviewer against\nthe same worktree. Use isolated worktrees when independent passes truly need to\nrun in parallel. Return concise role summaries and evidence to the primary\nagent instead of raw logs.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831778707,"completed_at_ms":1788831778707}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:58.973Z","ordinal":22144,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-631e6b99-caba-479e-a536-2a1d9b0a3c39","process_id":"13481","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: cakebrew-deliver\ndescription: Commit, publish, review, merge, and clean up a fully verified Cakebrew slice when the user explicitly requests the applicable delivery actions.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Deliver\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Delivery does not grant authority: perform only the\ncommit, push, PR or merge actions the user requested.\n\n- Confirm UI review when applicable, complete verification, and expert approval\n  all correspond to the current source state.\n- Reinspect the entire workspace and stage only the intended slice. Preserve\n  unrelated modifications and untracked files.\n- Create the atomic Conventional Commit required by `AGENTS.md`, including why\n  the change exists and what the test covers.\n- Open a ready PR with `gh` only when requested, reporting all verification and\n  any genuine gaps.\n- Wait for both CI jobs and every assigned human or automated review. Never\n  bypass pending, failing or requested-change gates.\n- Squash merge and clean up only with explicit merge authorization, including\n  the stacked-PR precaution in `AGENTS.md`.\n\nStop and report any stale gate evidence, changed head, failed CI, unresolved\nreview, authentication issue or authorization boundary.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-deliver\ndescription: Commit, publish, review, merge, and clean up a fully verified Cakebrew slice when the user explicitly requests the applicable delivery actions.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Deliver\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Delivery does not grant authority: perform only the\ncommit, push, PR or merge actions the user requested.\n\n- Confirm UI review when applicable, complete verification, and expert approval\n  all correspond to the current source state.\n- Reinspect the entire workspace and stage only the intended slice. Preserve\n  unrelated modifications and untracked files.\n- Create the atomic Conventional Commit required by `AGENTS.md`, including why\n  the change exists and what the test covers.\n- Open a ready PR with `gh` only when requested, reporting all verification and\n  any genuine gaps.\n- Wait for both CI jobs and every assigned human or automated review. Never\n  bypass pending, failing or requested-change gates.\n- Squash merge and clean up only with explicit merge authorization, including\n  the stacked-PR precaution in `AGENTS.md`.\n\nStop and report any stale gate evidence, changed head, failed CI, unresolved\nreview, authentication issue or authorization boundary.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6588},"formatted_output":"---\nname: cakebrew-deliver\ndescription: Commit, publish, review, merge, and clean up a fully verified Cakebrew slice when the user explicitly requests the applicable delivery actions.\n---\n\n# Cakebrew Deliver\n\nRead `AGENTS.md` completely. Delivery does not grant authority: perform only the\ncommit, push, PR or merge actions the user requested.\n\n- Confirm UI review when applicable, complete verification, and expert approval\n  all correspond to the current source state.\n- Reinspect the entire workspace and stage only the intended slice. Preserve\n  unrelated modifications and untracked files.\n- Create the atomic Conventional Commit required by `AGENTS.md`, including why\n  the change exists and what the test covers.\n- Open a ready PR with `gh` only when requested, reporting all verification and\n  any genuine gaps.\n- Wait for both CI jobs and every assigned human or automated review. Never\n  bypass pending, failing or requested-change gates.\n- Squash merge and clean up only with explicit merge authorization, including\n  the stacked-PR precaution in `AGENTS.md`.\n\nStop and report any stale gate evidence, changed head, failed CI, unresolved\nreview, authentication issue or authorization boundary.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831778973,"completed_at_ms":1788831778973}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:42:59.274Z","ordinal":22145,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3c9dc00f-bacd-487a-84a8-1b4396fe766b","process_id":"54665","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .codex/agents/cakebrew-planner.toml"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .codex/agents/cakebrew-planner.toml","name":"cakebrew-planner.toml","path":".codex/agents/cakebrew-planner.toml"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"name = \"cakebrew-planner\"\ndescription = \"Cakebrew discovery and planning specialist for spikes, architectural decisions, and thin vertical slice definition before implementation.\"\nsandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nRead AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\nInvoke $cakebrew-plan and stay in the planner role. Inspect and measure assumptions, compare alternatives, and return the smallest testable vertical slice with acceptance criteria and an expected red test.\nAny spike is disposable. Keep it isolated, remove it before returning, and never promote it into production code.\nDo not implement the slice, commit, push, open a PR, or modify project instructions. Preserve every unrelated change.\n\"\"\"\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"name = \"cakebrew-planner\"\ndescription = \"Cakebrew discovery and planning specialist for spikes, architectural decisions, and thin vertical slice definition before implementation.\"\nsandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nRead AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\nInvoke $cakebrew-plan and stay in the planner role. Inspect and measure assumptions, compare alternatives, and return the smallest testable vertical slice with acceptance criteria and an expected red test.\nAny spike is disposable. Keep it isolated, remove it before returning, and never promote it into production code.\nDo not implement the slice, commit, push, open a PR, or modify project instructions. Preserve every unrelated change.\n\"\"\"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12405},"formatted_output":"name = \"cakebrew-planner\"\ndescription = \"Cakebrew discovery and planning specialist for spikes, architectural decisions, and thin vertical slice definition before implementation.\"\nsandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nRead AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\nInvoke $cakebrew-plan and stay in the planner role. Inspect and measure assumptions, compare alternatives, and return the smallest testable vertical slice with acceptance criteria and an expected red test.\nAny spike is disposable. Keep it isolated, remove it before returning, and never promote it into production code.\nDo not implement the slice, commit, push, open a PR, or modify project instructions. Preserve every unrelated change.\n\"\"\"\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831779274,"completed_at_ms":1788831779274}}
