{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:43:00.328Z","ordinal":22149,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1d1e6445-cbfc-4063-b0dc-731438496938","process_id":"88998","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .codex/agents/cakebrew-code-reviewer.toml"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .codex/agents/cakebrew-code-reviewer.toml","name":"cakebrew-code-reviewer.toml","path":".codex/agents/cakebrew-code-reviewer.toml"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"name = \"cakebrew-code-reviewer\"\ndescription = \"Independent pre-commit Cakebrew reviewer focused on correctness, regressions, Objective-C/AppKit safety, architecture, and missing tests.\"\nsandbox_mode = \"read-only\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nRead AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\nInvoke $cakebrew-code-review. Review the full branch diff plus staged, unstaged, and untracked files after verification passes.\nDo not edit source files. Lead with actionable findings ordered by severity and include precise file and line evidence. Avoid style-only comments. Explicitly approve the gate when no actionable findings remain; route fixes to the implementer and require fresh verification afterward.\n\"\"\"\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"name = \"cakebrew-code-reviewer\"\ndescription = \"Independent pre-commit Cakebrew reviewer focused on correctness, regressions, Objective-C/AppKit safety, architecture, and missing tests.\"\nsandbox_mode = \"read-only\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nRead AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\nInvoke $cakebrew-code-review. Review the full branch diff plus staged, unstaged, and untracked files after verification passes.\nDo not edit source files. Lead with actionable findings ordered by severity and include precise file and line evidence. Avoid style-only comments. Explicitly approve the gate when no actionable findings remain; route fixes to the implementer and require fresh verification afterward.\n\"\"\"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4876},"formatted_output":"name = \"cakebrew-code-reviewer\"\ndescription = \"Independent pre-commit Cakebrew reviewer focused on correctness, regressions, Objective-C/AppKit safety, architecture, and missing tests.\"\nsandbox_mode = \"read-only\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nRead AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\nInvoke $cakebrew-code-review. Review the full branch diff plus staged, unstaged, and untracked files after verification passes.\nDo not edit source files. Lead with actionable findings ordered by severity and include precise file and line evidence. Avoid style-only comments. Explicitly approve the gate when no actionable findings remain; route fixes to the implementer and require fresh verification afterward.\n\"\"\"\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831780328,"completed_at_ms":1788831780328}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:43:00.585Z","ordinal":22150,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2e3c1d80-7d91-4f4a-8259-c0cebf2d7976","process_id":"95811","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat CONTRIBUTING.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat CONTRIBUTING.md","name":"CONTRIBUTING.md","path":"CONTRIBUTING.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Contributing\n\n**[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) is the single source of truth** for how work happens\nhere — the workflow, the conventions, and the decisions already made. It is\nwritten for human contributors and coding agents alike.\n\nThis file deliberately does not restate any of it. Two documents describing one\nworkflow drift apart, and then neither can be trusted.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) once, end to end. It is not long, and most of it\n   is things that cost someone a wasted afternoon to learn.\n2. Branch off `main`, take one thin slice, write the failing test first.\n3. Open a PR with `gh`. Green CI is the merge gate.\n\n## The commands you will need every time\n\n```sh\n# App build, both configurations — both must be warning-free\nxcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n  -configuration Debug -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\nxcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n  -configuration Release -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\n# Unit tests — seconds, run them every time\nxcodebuild test -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme CakebrewTests \\\n  -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\n# UI tests — a pre-PR step, not an inner-loop one (~8 minutes)\nxcodebuild test -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n```\n\nIf you touch `CakebrewUITests.m`, compile that target — neither test command\nabove does, so a syntax error there passes locally and fails on CI:\n\n```sh\nxcodebuild build-for-testing -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n```\n\n## Reporting bugs\n\nPlease use the issue templates. The environment questions are not boilerplate:\nthe macOS version, the Homebrew version and prefix, and whether the problem\nreproduces under `-BPMockBrew` are what separate a parser bug from an\nenvironment one.\n\nSecurity issues go through [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), not a public issue.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Contributing\n\n**[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) is the single source of truth** for how work happens\nhere — the workflow, the conventions, and the decisions already made. It is\nwritten for human contributors and coding agents alike.\n\nThis file deliberately does not restate any of it. Two documents describing one\nworkflow drift apart, and then neither can be trusted.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) once, end to end. It is not long, and most of it\n   is things that cost someone a wasted afternoon to learn.\n2. Branch off `main`, take one thin slice, write the failing test first.\n3. Open a PR with `gh`. Green CI is the merge gate.\n\n## The commands you will need every time\n\n```sh\n# App build, both configurations — both must be warning-free\nxcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n  -configuration Debug -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\nxcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n  -configuration Release -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\n# Unit tests — seconds, run them every time\nxcodebuild test -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme CakebrewTests \\\n  -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\n# UI tests — a pre-PR step, not an inner-loop one (~8 minutes)\nxcodebuild test -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n```\n\nIf you touch `CakebrewUITests.m`, compile that target — neither test command\nabove does, so a syntax error there passes locally and fails on CI:\n\n```sh\nxcodebuild build-for-testing -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n```\n\n## Reporting bugs\n\nPlease use the issue templates. The environment questions are not boilerplate:\nthe macOS version, the Homebrew version and prefix, and whether the problem\nreproduces under `-BPMockBrew` are what separate a parser bug from an\nenvironment one.\n\nSecurity issues go through [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), not a public issue.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7128},"formatted_output":"# Contributing\n\n**[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) is the single source of truth** for how work happens\nhere — the workflow, the conventions, and the decisions already made. It is\nwritten for human contributors and coding agents alike.\n\nThis file deliberately does not restate any of it. Two documents describing one\nworkflow drift apart, and then neither can be trusted.\n\n## Start here\n\n1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) once, end to end. It is not long, and most of it\n   is things that cost someone a wasted afternoon to learn.\n2. Branch off `main`, take one thin slice, write the failing test first.\n3. Open a PR with `gh`. Green CI is the merge gate.\n\n## The commands you will need every time\n\n```sh\n# App build, both configurations — both must be warning-free\nxcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n  -configuration Debug -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\nxcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n  -configuration Release -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\n# Unit tests — seconds, run them every time\nxcodebuild test -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme CakebrewTests \\\n  -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n\n# UI tests — a pre-PR step, not an inner-loop one (~8 minutes)\nxcodebuild test -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n```\n\nIf you touch `CakebrewUITests.m`, compile that target — neither test command\nabove does, so a syntax error there passes locally and fails on CI:\n\n```sh\nxcodebuild build-for-testing -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n```\n\n## Reporting bugs\n\nPlease use the issue templates. The environment questions are not boilerplate:\nthe macOS version, the Homebrew version and prefix, and whether the problem\nreproduces under `-BPMockBrew` are what separate a parser bug from an\nenvironment one.\n\nSecurity issues go through [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), not a public issue.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788831780585,"completed_at_ms":1788831780585}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:43:10.349Z","ordinal":22151,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-43cba07f-a970-47cc-aae7-132e3e54d80f","changes":{"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-ui-review/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,20 +2,11 @@\n name: cakebrew-ui-review\n-description: Review a user-visible Cakebrew change for AppKit conventions, layout, appearance, accessibility, and UI journey coverage after implementation stabilizes.\n+description: Independently review a stabilized user-visible Cakebrew change for AppKit layout, appearance, accessibility and UI journey coverage.\n ---\n-\n-# Cakebrew Ui Review\n \n-Read `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the changed surface independently; do not\n-edit source files.\n+# Cakebrew UI Review\n \n-- Inspect the branch and workspace diff to identify affected journeys.\n-- Launch against `-BPMockBrew` and verify the relevant state visually.\n-- Check layout, dark mode, badges, accessibility identity and macOS idioms.\n-- Prefer an existing or proposed `CakebrewUITests` assertion for behavior that\n-  should not depend on visual judgment.\n-- Account for the documented locked-screen and headless-CI limitations before\n-  classifying a failure.\n+Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n+project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Quality gates**\n+section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-Return prioritized, reproducible findings with file or UI location and expected\n-behavior. Say explicitly when the gate passes. Send fixes back to the\n-implementer rather than making them in the review pass.\n+Inspect the supplied diff and run the UI review defined in AGENTS.md using its testing contracts and environment diagnostics. Return observed evidence and a clear approval, actionable findings or blocker. Do not repair the implementation or mistake unavailable visual coverage for a pass.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-verifier.toml":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@\n name = \"cakebrew-verifier\"\n-description = \"Cakebrew verification specialist for warning-free Debug and Release builds, unit tests, UI target compilation, and UI journeys.\"\n+description = \"Independent source-matched Cakebrew build, test and diagnostic verification; reports failures without fixing them.\"\n sandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n developer_instructions = \"\"\"\n-Read AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\n-Invoke $cakebrew-verify and run the complete applicable verification gate from the beginning. Validate that each instrument exercised the intended target.\n-Do not edit source files. Separate real failures from sandbox, signing, locked-display, and headless-CI artifacts. Return compact command evidence and an explicit pass or fail; route failures to the implementer.\n+Read AGENTS.md completely before acting. It is the sole project authority; this agent is a role adapter, not a second workflow.\n+Invoke $cakebrew-verify. Follow the assignment, evidence and concurrency contracts in AGENTS.md.\n+Validate the assigned stable state using the applicable verification gate in AGENTS.md. You may generate build and test artifacts, but may not edit sources. Return the verifier handoff with actual execution evidence and pass, fail or blocked status. A runner failure or missing execution is not a passing product test.\n+Keep the assignment bounded. Do not change project policy or perform commit, publish, PR or merge actions unless explicitly assigned; gate agents never edit sources. Report missing inputs or authority to the primary agent.\n \"\"\"\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-plan/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,21 +2,11 @@\n name: cakebrew-plan\n-description: Plan or spike a Cakebrew change before implementation when requirements, architecture, framework behavior, integration boundaries, or vertical-slice scope need to be resolved.\n+description: Plan a Cakebrew change or spike when requirements, framework behavior, architectural tradeoffs or vertical-slice scope need resolution.\n ---\n \n-# Cakebrew Plan\n+# Cakebrew Planning\n \n-Read `AGENTS.md` completely. Stay in the planner role: do not implement\n-production code.\n+Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n+project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Discovery and scoping**\n+section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-- Inspect the repository and trace the relevant execution paths.\n-- Identify unknowns that require measurement. Use the smallest disposable\n-  spike needed, keep it out of production paths, and remove it before returning.\n-- Compare viable alternatives by architectural fit, complexity, performance\n-  and maintenance burden.\n-- Define the smallest cohesive vertical slice, its acceptance criteria, test\n-  seams and expected red test.\n-- Report assumptions, evidence, risks, rejected alternatives and an ordered\n-  slice plan. Clearly distinguish measured behavior from inference.\n-\n-Preserve all unrelated changes. Do not commit, push, open a PR or change\n-project instructions.\n+Read the assigned problem and trace the relevant code and tests. Return the planner handoff specified in AGENTS.md, distinguishing observations from assumptions and identifying what must be measured. Keep any authorized spike isolated and account for its cleanup; do not implement production changes.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-ui-reviewer.toml":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@\n name = \"cakebrew-ui-reviewer\"\n-description = \"Independent Cakebrew AppKit UI and UX reviewer for visual changes, accessibility, platform conventions, and UI journey coverage.\"\n+description = \"Independent AppKit visual, accessibility and journey review of a stable Cakebrew diff.\"\n sandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n developer_instructions = \"\"\"\n-Read AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\n-Invoke $cakebrew-ui-review. Review the implemented user-visible surface against the branch and workspace diff using the mock build and the repository's documented UI constraints.\n-Do not edit source files. Return reproducible findings ordered by impact, or explicitly approve the UI gate when no actionable findings remain. Route fixes to the implementer.\n+Read AGENTS.md completely before acting. It is the sole project authority; this agent is a role adapter, not a second workflow.\n+Invoke $cakebrew-ui-review. Follow the assignment, evidence and concurrency contracts in AGENTS.md.\n+Review the assigned stable diff using the UI gate and testing contracts in AGENTS.md. You may run builds and authorized mock UI checks but may not edit sources. Return the UI reviewer handoff with observed evidence and approval, actionable findings or an environment blocker.\n+Keep the assignment bounded. Do not change project policy or perform commit, publish, PR or merge actions unless explicitly assigned; gate agents never edit sources. Report missing inputs or authority to the primary agent.\n \"\"\"\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,3 +2,3 @@\n name: cakebrew-workflow\n-description: Orchestrate a complete Cakebrew feature, bugfix, or behavior-changing refactor through planning, TDD implementation, UI review when applicable, verification, expert review, and delivery gates.\n+description: Orchestrate a Cakebrew feature, bugfix or behavior-changing refactor across planning, implementation, independent quality gates and authorized delivery.\n ---\n@@ -6,26 +6,7 @@\n # Cakebrew Workflow\n-\n-Read `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole authority for the\n-workflow, commands, architecture and delivery rules; this skill only routes the\n-work through the configured roles.\n \n-1. Use `cakebrew-planner` with `$cakebrew-plan` to validate assumptions and\n-   define the smallest vertical slice. Any spike is disposable.\n-2. Inspect repository state, synchronize the latest `main`, preserve unrelated\n-   changes, and create the required branch before production edits.\n-3. Give `cakebrew-implementer` explicit ownership of the slice and invoke\n-   `$cakebrew-implement`. Require observed red-green-refactor evidence.\n-4. If a user-visible surface changed, run `cakebrew-ui-reviewer` with\n-   `$cakebrew-ui-review` after implementation is stable.\n-5. Run `cakebrew-verifier` with `$cakebrew-verify`, then\n-   `cakebrew-code-reviewer` with `$cakebrew-code-review`.\n-6. Route every actionable finding back to the implementer. After any source\n-   edit, repeat verification and expert review; repeat UI review too when the\n-   fix changes the visible surface.\n-7. Keep delivery with the primary agent. Invoke `$cakebrew-deliver` only when\n-   the user has authorized the relevant commit, push, PR or merge action.\n+Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n+project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Role orchestration and evidence**\n+section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-Do not run a mutating agent concurrently with a verifier or reviewer against\n-the same worktree. Use isolated worktrees when independent passes truly need to\n-run in parallel. Return concise role summaries and evidence to the primary\n-agent instead of raw logs.\n+Dispatch the configured roles in AGENTS.md lifecycle order with its assignment and handoff contracts. Keep requirements, cross-role decisions and delivery with the primary agent. Route findings through its fix loop and track which evidence is current; use its concurrency rules before overlapping work.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,24 +2,11 @@\n name: cakebrew-deliver\n-description: Commit, publish, review, merge, and clean up a fully verified Cakebrew slice when the user explicitly requests the applicable delivery actions.\n+description: Deliver a verified Cakebrew slice when the user authorizes committing, publishing, opening a PR or merging; coordinate any required remediation through the workflow.\n ---\n-\n-# Cakebrew Deliver\n \n-Read `AGENTS.md` completely. Delivery does not grant authority: perform only the\n-commit, push, PR or merge actions the user requested.\n+# Cakebrew Delivery\n \n-- Confirm UI review when applicable, complete verification, and expert approval\n-  all correspond to the current source state.\n-- Reinspect the entire workspace and stage only the intended slice. Preserve\n-  unrelated modifications and untracked files.\n-- Create the atomic Conventional Commit required by `AGENTS.md`, including why\n-  the change exists and what the test covers.\n-- Open a ready PR with `gh` only when requested, reporting all verification and\n-  any genuine gaps.\n-- Wait for both CI jobs and every assigned human or automated review. Never\n-  bypass pending, failing or requested-change gates.\n-- Squash merge and clean up only with explicit merge authorization, including\n-  the stacked-PR precaution in `AGENTS.md`.\n+Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n+project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Delivery**\n+section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-Stop and report any stale gate evidence, changed head, failed CI, unresolved\n-review, authentication issue or authorization boundary.\n+Apply only the authorized delivery stages in AGENTS.md. Check source-matched gate evidence before mutation, and use its CI, assigned-review, stacked-PR and cleanup rules. Route stale evidence or in-scope findings back through $cakebrew-workflow; hold the affected delivery stage. Report genuine authority or environment blockers without silently bypassing gates.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-planner.toml":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n name = \"cakebrew-planner\"\n-description = \"Cakebrew discovery and planning specialist for spikes, architectural decisions, and thin vertical slice definition before implementation.\"\n+description = \"Discovery and planning for one Cakebrew slice; measures unknowns and returns an implementation handoff.\"\n sandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n developer_instructions = \"\"\"\n-Read AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\n-Invoke $cakebrew-plan and stay in the planner role. Inspect and measure assumptions, compare alternatives, and return the smallest testable vertical slice with acceptance criteria and an expected red test.\n-Any spike is disposable. Keep it isolated, remove it before returning, and never promote it into production code.\n-Do not implement the slice, commit, push, open a PR, or modify project instructions. Preserve every unrelated change.\n+Read AGENTS.md completely before acting. It is the sole project authority; this agent is a role adapter, not a second workflow.\n+Invoke $cakebrew-plan. Follow the assignment, evidence and concurrency contracts in AGENTS.md.\n+Work from the assigned problem and repository evidence. Own only the explicitly assigned planning/spike artifacts. Return measured findings, alternatives and the planner handoff required by AGENTS.md; identify assumptions and cleanup. Do not implement production changes.\n+Keep the assignment bounded. Do not change project policy or perform commit, publish, PR or merge actions unless explicitly assigned; gate agents never edit sources. Report missing inputs or authority to the primary agent.\n \"\"\"\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-code-review/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,19 +2,11 @@\n name: cakebrew-code-review\n-description: Perform the independent pre-commit expert review of a Cakebrew branch and all uncommitted files after verification passes.\n+description: Independently review a verified Cakebrew branch and all uncommitted files before commit, or re-review after fixes invalidate approval.\n ---\n \n-# Cakebrew Code Review\n+# Cakebrew Expert Code Review\n \n-Read `AGENTS.md` completely. Review the full branch diff against its base plus\n-all staged, unstaged and untracked files. Do not edit source files.\n+Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n+project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Quality gates**\n+section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-Prioritize correctness, regressions, Objective-C and AppKit idioms, memory and\n-concurrency safety, performance, architecture, edge cases, mock fidelity and\n-missing tests. Trace the actual execution path before reporting a problem.\n-Avoid style-only comments unless they reveal a concrete maintenance or defect\n-risk.\n-\n-Return findings ordered by severity with precise file and line references,\n-impact and a reproducible rationale. If there are no actionable findings, say\n-the gate is approved. Any fix belongs to the implementer and invalidates the\n-prior verification result.\n+Require current verification evidence, then inspect the full review scope defined in AGENTS.md. Return approval or actionable findings with severity, file/line, impact and supporting evidence. Include untracked and unrelated workspace changes in inspection without expanding the slice or editing files.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-verify/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,22 +2,11 @@\n name: cakebrew-verify\n-description: Run Cakebrew's complete local verification gate after implementation or fixes, including required builds, tests, warnings checks, and UI-target coverage.\n+description: Validate a stabilized Cakebrew slice with the complete applicable verification gate and source-matched evidence, without editing source.\n ---\n \n-# Cakebrew Verify\n-\n-Read `AGENTS.md` completely and use its current commands as the authority. Do\n-not edit source files.\n-\n-Run the gate from the beginning in its documented order:\n+# Cakebrew Verification\n \n-1. Debug build, warning-free.\n-2. Release build, warning-free.\n-3. Full unit suite.\n-4. UI test target compilation.\n-5. UI journeys before PR creation, subject to the documented display checks.\n+Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n+project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Quality gates**\n+section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-Validate that each instrument actually exercised the intended target; do not\n-treat an exit code or silent output alone as proof. Separate genuine product or\n-setup failures from sandbox, signing, locked-screen or headless-environment\n-artifacts. Return a compact command-by-command result with decisive diagnostics\n-and an explicit pass/fail. Route failures to the implementer.\n+Run the applicable verification gate using AGENTS.md commands and testing contracts. Return commands, source identity, diagnostics, executed counts/skips and evidence paths. Distinguish product failures from environment blockers. Report pass, fail or blocked without fixing sources or waiving checks.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-implementer.toml":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n name = \"cakebrew-implementer\"\n-description = \"Cakebrew implementation specialist for one explicitly assigned vertical slice under strict red-green-refactor TDD.\"\n+description = \"Implementation of one explicitly owned Cakebrew slice with observed TDD evidence; no self-approval or delivery.\"\n sandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n developer_instructions = \"\"\"\n-Read AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\n-Invoke $cakebrew-implement. You own only the files and behavior explicitly assigned by the primary agent. You are not alone in the codebase: preserve unrelated work and accommodate concurrent changes without reverting them.\n-Observe the focused test fail for the expected reason before production implementation, then make the minimum change, refactor green, and inspect the whole workspace diff.\n-Return changed files and red-green-refactor evidence. Do not approve your own UI, verification, or code-review gates. Never commit or publish; delivery belongs to the primary agent.\n+Read AGENTS.md completely before acting. It is the sole project authority; this agent is a role adapter, not a second workflow.\n+Invoke $cakebrew-implement. Follow the assignment, evidence and concurrency contracts in AGENTS.md.\n+Confirm the assigned worktree, acceptance criteria and file ownership. You are not alone in the codebase: preserve other agents' and the user's changes. Return the implementer handoff required by AGENTS.md, including expected-failure and passing-test evidence. Return findings to the primary agent instead of approving your own work.\n+Keep the assignment bounded. Do not change project policy or perform commit, publish, PR or merge actions unless explicitly assigned; gate agents never edit sources. Report missing inputs or authority to the primary agent.\n \"\"\"\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-implement/SKILL.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,20 +2,11 @@\n name: cakebrew-implement\n-description: Implement an assigned Cakebrew vertical slice under strict red-green-refactor TDD after its scope and acceptance criteria are established.\n+description: Implement one scoped Cakebrew feature, bugfix or behavior-changing refactor under red-green-refactor TDD, including fixes returned by quality gates.\n ---\n-\n-# Cakebrew Implement\n \n-Read `AGENTS.md` completely and accept explicit ownership of the assigned files\n-or behavior. Other work may exist in the checkout; never revert or absorb it.\n+# Cakebrew Implementation\n \n-1. Confirm the slice, acceptance criteria and intended test seam.\n-2. Add the smallest focused test first and run it to observe the expected red.\n-3. Implement only enough production code to make it green.\n-4. Refactor with the focused test and relevant fast suite green.\n-5. Inspect all staged, unstaged and untracked files and remove scratch or debug\n-   artifacts created by this implementation.\n+Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n+project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Implementation**\n+section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-If red was not observed, perform and report the mutation proof required by\n-`AGENTS.md`. Stop after implementation evidence; do not self-approve the UI,\n-verification or expert-review gates. Never commit or publish; delivery belongs\n-to the primary agent under `$cakebrew-deliver`.\n+Use the assigned acceptance criteria and file ownership. Return the implementer handoff specified in AGENTS.md, including actual expected-failure evidence and the resulting diff. Flag missing scope before expanding it. Leave gate decisions and delivery to their assigned roles.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/CONTRIBUTING.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,52 +2,6 @@\n \n-**[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) is the single source of truth** for how work happens\n-here — the workflow, the conventions, and the decisions already made. It is\n-written for human contributors and coding agents alike.\n-\n-This file deliberately does not restate any of it. Two documents describing one\n-workflow drift apart, and then neither can be trusted.\n-\n-## Start here\n-\n-1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) once, end to end. It is not long, and most of it\n-   is things that cost someone a wasted afternoon to learn.\n-2. Branch off `main`, take one thin slice, write the failing test first.\n-3. Open a PR with `gh`. Green CI is the merge gate.\n-\n-## The commands you will need every time\n-\n-```sh\n-# App build, both configurations — both must be warning-free\n-xcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n-  -configuration Debug -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n-\n-xcodebuild build -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme Cakebrew \\\n-  -configuration Release -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n+Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the authoritative workflow, build and test\n+commands, conventions and architecture decisions for Cakebrew.\n \n-# Unit tests — seconds, run them every time\n-xcodebuild test -workspace Cakebrew.xcworkspace -scheme CakebrewTests \\\n-  -destination 'platform=macOS' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO\n-\n-# UI tests — a pre-PR step, not an inner-loop one (~8 minutes)\n-xcodebuild test -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n-  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n-  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n-```\n-\n-If you touch `CakebrewUITests.m`, compile that target — neither test command\n-above does, so a syntax error there passes locally and fails on CI:\n-\n-```sh\n-xcodebuild build-for-testing -scheme CakebrewUITests -destination 'platform=macOS' \\\n-  CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=\"-\" CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO \\\n-  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=\"\" PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER=\"\"\n-```\n-\n-## Reporting bugs\n-\n-Please use the issue templates. The environment questions are not boilerplate:\n-the macOS version, the Homebrew version and prefix, and whether the problem\n-reproduces under `-BPMockBrew` are what separate a parser bug from an\n-environment one.\n-\n-Security issues go through [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), not a public issue.\n+Use the repository's issue templates to report bugs or propose improvements.\n+Report security concerns through [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), not a public issue.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-code-reviewer.toml":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@\n name = \"cakebrew-code-reviewer\"\n-description = \"Independent pre-commit Cakebrew reviewer focused on correctness, regressions, Objective-C/AppKit safety, architecture, and missing tests.\"\n+description = \"Independent pre-commit review of the full verified Cakebrew branch and workspace diff; read-only findings or approval.\"\n sandbox_mode = \"read-only\"\n developer_instructions = \"\"\"\n-Read AGENTS.md completely before acting; it is the sole authority for this repository.\n-Invoke $cakebrew-code-review. Review the full branch diff plus staged, unstaged, and untracked files after verification passes.\n-Do not edit source files. Lead with actionable findings ordered by severity and include precise file and line evidence. Avoid style-only comments. Explicitly approve the gate when no actionable findings remain; route fixes to the implementer and require fresh verification afterward.\n+Read AGENTS.md completely before acting. It is the sole project authority; this agent is a role adapter, not a second workflow.\n+Invoke $cakebrew-code-review. Follow the assignment, evidence and concurrency contracts in AGENTS.md.\n+Inspect the full assigned branch and workspace diff after confirming current verification evidence. Apply the expert review gate in AGENTS.md and return its code-reviewer handoff. Stay read-only; report actionable findings or approval, never silently fix or waive a finding.\n+Keep the assignment bounded. Do not change project policy or perform commit, publish, PR or merge actions unless explicitly assigned; gate agents never edit sources. Report missing inputs or authority to the primary agent.\n \"\"\"\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-plan/SKILL.md\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-implement/SKILL.md\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-ui-review/SKILL.md\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-verify/SKILL.md\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-code-review/SKILL.md\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-planner.toml\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-implementer.toml\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-ui-reviewer.toml\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-verifier.toml\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/.codex/agents/cakebrew-code-reviewer.toml\nM /Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/CONTRIBUTING.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788831781960,"completed_at_ms":1788831790349}}
