{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:44:56.312Z","ordinal":22217,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a07eb0-92f8-75e2-be66-36eb44e68a21","author":"/root/search_ui_gates","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/search_ui_gates\nPayload:\nRead current AGENTS.md, all seven skills, and all five agent adapters on `docs/agent-workflow`. No actionable contradictions or missing routes emerged in these six dry runs.\n\n1. **CI helper crash despite local pass:** Hold merge. Diagnose current-head crash evidence without assuming infrastructure. Route an in-scope compatibility fix to the implementer, prove the relevant regression, rerun the complete verification sequence, and obtain fresh independent expert approval. Repeat UI review if the fix changes a user-facing surface. Publish the reviewed fix under existing authority, then require current-head CI and assigned approvals before squash merge. A runner crash alone is not TDD red. [AGENTS.md:53](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:53), [AGENTS.md:91](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:91), [AGENTS.md:109](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:109)\n\n2. **UI reviewer offers to patch during verification:** Reject that role overlap and concurrent mutation. Reviewer returns the layout finding; primary releases the stable-source gate assignment before assigning the implementer. Following the fix: fresh UI review, complete verification, then independent expert review. Delivery cannot proceed on the previous evidence. [AGENTS.md:69](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:69), [AGENTS.md:148](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:148)\n\n3. **Two worktrees need UI journeys simultaneously:** Serialize runtime/display ownership unless every shared resource is genuinely isolated. Separate worktrees and derived data are insufficient. Preserve and restore preferences/cache/app state between owners; independent compilation can remain parallel with separate derived data. Neither slice may borrow the other’s results. [AGENTS.md:154](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:154)\n\n4. **Test and implementation written together; zero tests executed:** Neither red nor green is established. Correct test discovery/execution first; then deliberately mutate the implementation and observe the intended assertion failure, restore it, confirm real passing execution, and complete applicable gates. `TEST SUCCEEDED` alone cannot authorize delivery. [AGENTS.md:53](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:53), [AGENTS.md:190](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:190)\n\n5. **Only behavior-fix authorization; verified implementation wants publication:** Report the completed verified/reviewed change and request delivery authorization. Do not infer commit, push, PR, or merge authority from implementation approval. [AGENTS.md:99](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:99)\n\n6. **Instruction-only adapters versus CI YAML:** The adapter rewrite uses syntax, link, routing validation and independent policy review—not app builds as proof of prose correctness. The primary assigns those applicable checks to independent verification/review roles. A CI change is explicitly excluded from that exception: full applicable executable verification remains required; behavior-changing CI logic also needs meaningful regression evidence. Both still need authorized delivery and current-head required CI before merge. [AGENTS.md:78](/Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew/AGENTS.md:78)\n\nThe adapters consistently defer these decisions to AGENTS.md: workflow/delivery route findings back; implementer owns repairs; gate agents report without editing. This approves the **scenario interpretation**, not syntax validation, live agent execution, or delivery readiness."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","create_time":1788831896.312277}}}
