{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:45:02.329Z","ordinal":22220,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f689d4ab487d1b7e21ad7237d42b3","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Syntax and routing checks passed, and the independent dry runs found no contradictions in the six scenarios. The Skill Creator validator lacked PyYAML, so I checked YAML with Ruby’s parser and TOML with Python’s parser instead. Independent policy review is the remaining check.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788831901292,"completed_at_ms":1788831902329}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:45:02.339Z","ordinal":22221,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f689d4ab487d1b7e21ad7237d42b3","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Syntax and routing checks passed, and the independent dry runs found no contradictions in the six scenarios. The Skill Creator validator lacked PyYAML, so I checked YAML with Ruby’s parser and TOML with Python’s parser instead. Independent policy review is the remaining check.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:45:04.154Z","ordinal":22222,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f689e65c887d1b5f90fefb732711d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_E4orWzyBD4BtBdEHA5LFRliB","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --binary -- AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md .agents/skills .codex/agents | shasum -a 256\\ngit show HEAD:AGENTS.md | wc -l\\nwc -l AGENTS.md\\nnl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '65,170p'\\ngit diff --name-only -- .github Cakebrew CakebrewTests CakebrewUITests .codex/config.toml .codex/agents/entire-search.toml\",max_output_tokens:2200}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","create_time":1788831898.417039}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:45:04.235Z","ordinal":22223,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","session_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","root_turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","response_id":"resp_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f6899c5cc87d18a0d44ef73d2e515","usage":{"input_tokens":84795,"cached_input_tokens":83456,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":263,"reasoning_output_tokens":75,"total_tokens":85058},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2139264,"cached_input_tokens":2021888,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":22246,"reasoning_output_tokens":1601,"total_tokens":2161510},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":299335359,"cached_input_tokens":295341696,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":563160,"reasoning_output_tokens":195821,"total_tokens":299898519}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T01:45:04.369Z","ordinal":22224,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ea9-3b2d-7200-b64b-ccfecb9fc7fb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a1f7f3b7-30b7-497c-93b2-d3cdd38f0881","process_id":"87276","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff --binary -- AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md .agents/skills .codex/agents | shasum -a 256\ngit show HEAD:AGENTS.md | wc -l\nwc -l AGENTS.md\nnl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '65,170p'\ngit diff --name-only -- .github Cakebrew CakebrewTests CakebrewUITests .codex/config.toml .codex/agents/entire-search.toml"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff --binary -- AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md .agents/skills .codex/agents | shasum -a 256\ngit show HEAD:AGENTS.md | wc -l\nwc -l AGENTS.md\nnl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '65,170p'\ngit diff --name-only -- .github Cakebrew CakebrewTests CakebrewUITests .codex/config.toml .codex/agents/entire-search.toml"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"faec16d94a4a5c6c0657032a58b833c60e17849acd19a305fa23d52e7ba047ca  -\n     475\n     302 AGENTS.md\n    65\t   changes and exclude them from the slice.\n    66\t\n    67\t### Quality gates — steps 6–8\n    68\t\n    69\tRun these gates in order on stable sources. Reviewers receive the actual diff\n    70\tand observed evidence, not just implementation intent. They report findings;\n    71\tthey do not fix their own findings.\n    72\t\n    73\t6. **UI/UX review, when user-visible behavior or appearance changes.** A\n    74\t   separate reviewer launches the mock build (`-BPMockBrew`) and checks layout,\n    75\t   light/dark appearance, badges, accessibility and AppKit idioms. Behavior\n    76\t   needs a `CakebrewUITests` journey, not screenshots alone. Report anything\n    77\t   that could not be exercised; an environment limitation is not an approval.\n    78\t7. **Verification.** Build Debug and Release warning-free, run the full unit\n    79\t   suite and applicable integration checks, compile the UI test target, and\n    80\t   run the full UI journeys before opening the PR. Inspect diagnostics and\n    81\t   static-analysis results; every warning or failed check is a finding.\n    82\t   Confirm tests actually executed against the intended source and binary.\n    83\t   For instruction/documentation-only changes, use syntax, link and routing\n    84\t   validation plus independent policy review; app builds do not validate prose.\n    85\t   This exception does not cover executable code, tests or build/CI changes.\n    86\t8. **Independent expert review.** Review the full branch diff and all\n    87\t   uncommitted files after verification passes. Cover Objective-C idioms,\n    88\t   memory and async safety, performance, architecture, edge cases, regressions\n    89\t   and missing tests. Resolve every actionable finding before approval.\n    90\t\n    91\t**Fix loop:** send findings to the implementer. After any code or test edit,\n    92\trestart the entire verification sequence and obtain fresh expert approval;\n    93\trepeat UI review when the fix changes a user-facing surface. No partial rerun\n    94\tor prior approval substitutes for gates on the changed state. Updated policy\n    95\tor instructions likewise need fresh applicable validation and review.\n    96\t\n    97\t### Delivery — steps 9–11\n    98\t\n    99\tThe primary agent owns delivery. Perform only the commit, publish, PR and merge\n   100\tactions the user has authorized; completing a stage does not authorize the next.\n   101\t\n   102\t9. **Atomic Conventional Commit.** Stage only the verified, reviewed slice.\n   103\t   Use `<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>` with type `feat`, `fix`,\n   104\t   `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `test`, `perf`, `build` or `ci`. The body explains\n   105\t   why and names the test coverage. Do not rewrite historical conventions.\n   106\t10. **Ready PR using `gh`.** No web UI; no draft unless requested. Explain\n   107\t    what changed, why, red-first or mutation evidence, verification results\n   108\t    and any unverified behavior with its reason.\n   109\t11. **Gated squash merge.** All required CI must be green, including both\n   110\t    **Build & Test** and **UI Tests**, for the current PR head. Wait for every\n   111\t    assigned human or automated review to approve and resolve actionable\n   112\t    feedback. Never bypass pending, failing or requested-change gates.\n   113\t\n   114\tDuring delivery, diagnose failures and route in-scope code/test fixes through\n   115\tthe fix loop; hold publication or merge until its gates pass. Stale evidence\n   116\trequires revalidation, not abandonment of the task. Stop for missing authority,\n   117\tcredentials, required user interaction or scope expansion. Do not treat an\n   118\tenvironment failure as a product defect or silently waive a gate.\n   119\t\n   120\tFor a CI UI failure, read the assertion and `CAKEBREW_UI_TREE_*` dump in the\n   121\tjob log before calling it flaky. Rerun once only when evidence indicates\n   122\tinfrastructure; otherwise fix the cause through the workflow.\n   123\t\n   124\tBefore deleting a stacked PR's parent branch, retarget the child PR to `main`;\n   125\tdeletion otherwise auto-closes it. Recheck the child's diff and gates against\n   126\tits new base. Merge with `gh pr merge <n> --squash --delete-branch`, then switch\n   127\tto `main` and `git pull --ff-only`, preserving unrelated work and respecting\n   128\tbranches checked out in other worktrees.\n   129\t\n   130\t## Role orchestration and evidence\n   131\t\n   132\tFor each feature, bugfix or behavior-changing refactor, the primary agent uses\n   133\t`$cakebrew-workflow` and delegates to the configured roles below. Planning,\n   134\timplementation and gates must not collapse into one self-review. If a custom\n   135\tagent is unavailable, use a separate agent with its matching skill; disclose\n   136\tany unavailable gate rather than claiming it passed.\n   137\t\n   138\t| Role | Skill | Custom agent | Required handoff |\n   139\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   140\t| Orchestrator | `$cakebrew-workflow` | Primary | Scope, decisions, role sequencing, authorized delivery |\n   141\t| Planner | `$cakebrew-plan` | `cakebrew-planner` | Measured unknowns, alternatives, ordered slices, acceptance criteria, expected red, spike cleanup |\n   142\t| Implementer | `$cakebrew-implement` | `cakebrew-implementer` | Owned diff, red/green or mutation evidence, remaining risks |\n   143\t| UI reviewer | `$cakebrew-ui-review` | `cakebrew-ui-reviewer` | Observed visual/journey evidence; approval, findings or blocker |\n   144\t| Verifier | `$cakebrew-verify` | `cakebrew-verifier` | Commands, diagnostics, test counts/skips, artifacts; pass, fail or blocker |\n   145\t| Code reviewer | `$cakebrew-code-review` | `cakebrew-code-reviewer` | Approval or actionable findings with severity, file/line, impact and evidence |\n   146\t| Delivery | `$cakebrew-deliver` | Primary | Commit/PR/head identity, CI and assigned-review status, merge/cleanup result |\n   147\t\n   148\tGive each assignment its worktree, base/head and uncommitted diff, acceptance\n   149\tcriteria, explicit file ownership, evidence locations and exclusions. Tell\n   150\tmutating agents they are not alone and must preserve others' edits. Subagents\n   151\tmay not expand scope, edit project policy or perform delivery unless those\n   152\tactions are explicitly their assignment. Gate agents never edit sources.\n   153\t\n   154\tHandoffs must identify the state examined: worktree, base/head and relevant\n   155\tuncommitted file state. Include concise observed results and log/artifact paths,\n   156\tnot raw log floods. A result for another tree or stale binary is not evidence.\n   157\t\n   158\t**Safe concurrency:** use isolated worktrees for independent mutating work.\n   159\tNever change sources while a verifier or reviewer examines that workspace.\n   160\tSeparate derived-data directories do not isolate the app's `NSUserDefaults`,\n   161\tcatalog cache, running process, `/Applications/Cakebrew.app` or display.\n   162\tSerialize UI/runtime work unless those resources are safely isolated. Preserve\n   163\tand restore user state; do not replace the installed app as incidental testing.\n   164\t\n   165\t## Build and test commands\n   166\t\n   167\tUse a separate `-derivedDataPath` per concurrent build/worktree. Select the\n   168\tintended architecture explicitly if Xcode reports ambiguous destinations.\n   169\tRun the following sequence for executable changes:\n   170\t\n.codex/config.toml\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"faec16d94a4a5c6c0657032a58b833c60e17849acd19a305fa23d52e7ba047ca  -\n     475\n     302 AGENTS.md\n    65\t   changes and exclude them from the slice.\n    66\t\n    67\t### Quality gates — steps 6–8\n    68\t\n    69\tRun these gates in order on stable sources. Reviewers receive the actual diff\n    70\tand observed evidence, not just implementation intent. They report findings;\n    71\tthey do not fix their own findings.\n    72\t\n    73\t6. **UI/UX review, when user-visible behavior or appearance changes.** A\n    74\t   separate reviewer launches the mock build (`-BPMockBrew`) and checks layout,\n    75\t   light/dark appearance, badges, accessibility and AppKit idioms. Behavior\n    76\t   needs a `CakebrewUITests` journey, not screenshots alone. Report anything\n    77\t   that could not be exercised; an environment limitation is not an approval.\n    78\t7. **Verification.** Build Debug and Release warning-free, run the full unit\n    79\t   suite and applicable integration checks, compile the UI test target, and\n    80\t   run the full UI journeys before opening the PR. Inspect diagnostics and\n    81\t   static-analysis results; every warning or failed 