{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T02:17:17.303Z","ordinal":22432,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ecd-5860-7493-96ec-54998be34ff0","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-c20331ab-d435-4179-b5d7-dd33da544db5","query":"Codex subagents parallel AGENTS instructions","action":{"type":"search","query":"Codex subagents parallel AGENTS instructions","queries":null},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn33search0","snippet":"`You should infer the user's intent and task scope from the instructions and prior conversation context. ... GPT-6 Astra is trained to be able to","title":"Model guidance | OpenAI API","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search1","snippet":"Usa subagentes en ChatGPT y Codex, y configura agentes personalizados de Codex ... `Review this branch with parallel subagents. ... * `developer_instructions` ... `agents.default_subagent_model` |","title":"Subagentes | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/es-419/docs/agent-configuration/subagents"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search2","snippet":"# Config profiles are separate files under CODEX_HOME. ... # Agents (multi-agent roles and limits) ... # default_subagent_model = \"gpt-5.6-terra\"","title":"Exemplo de configuração | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/pt-BR/docs/config-file/config-sample"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search3","snippet":"ChatGPT Work und Codex können Arbeitsabläufe mit Subagenten ausführen, indem sie spezialisierte Agenten parallel starten und deren Ergebnisse anschließend in einer Antwort zusammenfassen. ... `Review","title":"Subagenten | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/de-DE/docs/agent-configuration/subagents"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search4","snippet":"在 ChatGPT 和 Codex 中使用子智能体，并配置自定义 Codex 智能体 ... `Review this branch with parallel subagents. ... * `developer_instructions` ... `agents.default_subagent_model` | 字符串 | 否 | 设置所启动智能体的默认模型。","title":"子智能体 | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/zh-Hans/docs/agent-configuration/subagents"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search5","snippet":"Use subagentes no ChatGPT e no Codex e configure agentes personalizados do Codex ... `Review this branch with parallel subagents. ... * `developer_instructions` ... `agents.default_subagent_model`","title":"Subagentes | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/pt-BR/docs/agent-configuration/subagents"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search6","snippet":"Par exemple, Codex peut décomposer l’analyse d’un document de plusieurs millions de tokens en problèmes plus petits, puis renvoyer une synthèse des principaux enseignements au","title":"Sous-agents | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/fr-FR/docs/agent-configuration/subagents"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search7","snippet":"# Config profiles are separate files under CODEX_HOME. ... # Agents (multi-agent roles and limits) ... # default_subagent_model = \"gpt-5.6-terra\"","title":"Beispielkonfiguration | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/de-DE/docs/config-file/config-sample"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search8","snippet":"`npx @openai/codex-security scan . --diff origin/main --head HEAD` ... `--subagents N` | Sous-agents disponibles pour chaque worker.","title":"Référence de la CLI Codex Security | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/fr-FR/docs/security/cli/reference"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search9","snippet":"Cómo personalizar Codex con directrices del proyecto, habilidades, MCP y subagentes ... `AGENTS.md` define el comportamiento, las memorias conservan el contexto local para trabajos futuros,","title":"Personalización | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/es-419/docs/customization/overview"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search10","snippet":"Codex mit Projektanweisungen, Skills, MCP und Subagenten anpassen ... Mit `AGENTS.md` erhält Codex dauerhafte Projektanweisungen, die mit deinem Repository weitergegeben werden und schon gelten, bevor","title":"Anpassung | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/de-DE/docs/customization/overview"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"learn.chatgpt.com","ref_id":"turn33search11","snippet":"커스텀 에이전트를 직접 정의하려면 개인용 에이전트는 `~/.codex/agents/`에, 프로젝트 범위의 에이전트는 `.codex/agents/`에 독립된 TOML 파일을 추가하세요. ... * `developer_instructions`","title":"하위 에이전트 | ChatGPT Learn","url":"https://learn.chatgpt.com/ko-KR/docs/agent-configuration/subagents"}]},"started_at_ms":1788833835962,"completed_at_ms":1788833837302}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T02:17:17.795Z","ordinal":22433,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a055ce-e4d9-77c1-ac18-0944a8c71200","turn_id":"01a07ecd-5860-7493-96ec-54998be34ff0","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bca1040b-036d-466f-9947-c928711e5184","process_id":"37523","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff --check && ruby - <<'RUBY'\nrequire 'yaml'\nDir['.agents/skills/cakebrew-*/SKILL.md'].each do |path|\n  content = File.read(path)\n  data = YAML.safe_load(content.match(/\\A---\\n(.*?)\\n---/m)[1])\n  raise path unless data['name'] == File.basename(File.dirname(path)) && data['description'].is_a?(String) && data['description'].length.between?(1,1024)\n  raise path if data['description'].match?(/[<>]/) || content.include?('[TODO:')\nend\nputs 'All seven skill YAML frontmatters valid'\nRUBY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib, tomllib\nfor path in pathlib.Path('.codex/agents').glob('cakebrew-*.toml'):\n    data = tomllib.loads(path.read_text())\n    assert data['name'] == path.stem\n    assert 'AGENTS.md' in data['developer_instructions']\nprint('All five unchanged custom agents valid and routed to AGENTS.md')\nPY\ngit diff -- AGENTS.md .agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md .agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/cakebrew","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff --check && ruby - <<'RUBY'\nrequire 'yaml'\nDir['.agents/skills/cakebrew-*/SKILL.md'].each do |path|\n  content = File.read(path)\n  data = YAML.safe_load(content.match(/\\A---\\n(.*?)\\n---/m)[1])\n  raise path unless data['name'] == File.basename(File.dirname(path)) && data['description'].is_a?(String) && data['description'].length.between?(1,1024)\n  raise path if data['description'].match?(/[<>]/) || content.include?('[TODO:')\nend\nputs 'All seven skill YAML frontmatters valid'\nRUBY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib, tomllib\nfor path in pathlib.Path('.codex/agents').glob('cakebrew-*.toml'):\n    data = tomllib.loads(path.read_text())\n    assert data['name'] == path.stem\n    assert 'AGENTS.md' in data['developer_instructions']\nprint('All five unchanged custom agents valid and routed to AGENTS.md')\nPY\ngit diff -- AGENTS.md .agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md .agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"All seven skill YAML frontmatters valid\nAll five unchanged custom agents valid and routed to AGENTS.md\ndiff --git a/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md\nindex a4b2dd5..ba14938 100644\n--- a/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n ---\n name: cakebrew-deliver\n-description: Deliver a verified Cakebrew slice when the user authorizes committing, publishing, opening a PR or merging; coordinate any required remediation through the workflow.\n+description: Deliver a verified Cakebrew slice under a user-assigned goal or explicit delivery request, including gated squash merge and remediation within the authorized scope.\n ---\n \n # Cakebrew Delivery\n@@ -9,4 +9,9 @@ Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Delivery**\n section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-Apply only the authorized delivery stages in AGENTS.md. Check source-matched gate evidence before mutation, and use its CI, assigned-review, stacked-PR and cleanup rules. Route stale evidence or in-scope findings back through $cakebrew-workflow; hold the affected delivery stage. Report genuine authority or environment blockers without silently bypassing gates.\n+Apply AGENTS.md's goal authority and explicit user limits. Check source-matched\n+gate evidence before mutation, then carry authorized delivery through its CI,\n+assigned-review, squash-merge and cleanup rules without asking again at each\n+stage. Route stale evidence or in-scope findings through $cakebrew-workflow;\n+hold the affected delivery stage while remediation or external gates complete.\n+Follow AGENTS.md's stopping conditions for genuine blockers and resource pauses.\ndiff --git a/.agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md\nindex 4dcd5c5..8f79e16 100644\n--- a/.agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.agents/skills/cakebrew-workflow/SKILL.md\n@@ -9,4 +9,9 @@ Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sole\n project authority; this skill is a routing adapter. Follow its **Role orchestration and evidence**\n section and the assigned role's evidence contract, not a separate checklist here.\n \n-Dispatch the configured roles in AGENTS.md lifecycle order with its assignment and handoff contracts. Keep requirements, cross-role decisions and delivery with the primary agent. Route findings through its fix loop and track which evidence is current; use its concurrency rules before overlapping work.\n+Dispatch the configured roles using AGENTS.md's goal authority, lifecycle and\n+handoff contracts. Schedule independent work in parallel under its isolation\n+rules while preserving each slice's gate order. Keep requirements, cross-role\n+decisions and delivery with the primary agent. Route findings through its fix\n+loop, track current evidence and continue to the authorized goal's completion\n+without repeated stage approvals; honor its stopping conditions and user limits.\ndiff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nindex 00a449d..0a63dcc 100644\n--- a/AGENTS.md\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -96,8 +96,22 @@ or instructions likewise need fresh applicable validation and review.\n \n ### Delivery — steps 9–11\n \n-The primary agent owns delivery. Perform only the commit, publish, PR and merge\n-actions the user has authorized; completing a stage does not authorize the next.\n+The primary agent owns delivery. A user-assigned implementation or delivery\n+goal authorizes the in-scope lifecycle through commits, pushes, ready PRs,\n+gated squash merges and cleanup. Do not ask for renewed permission at each\n+stage or stop at an intermediate handoff when the goal remains unfinished.\n+An explicit limit such as \"plan only\", \"review only\", \"do not push\" or\n+\"leave the PR open\" overrides this default; questions and diagnosis alone\n+do not authorize implementation or delivery.\n+\n+Continue through the goal's scoped slices, resolve in-scope findings and repeat\n+invalidated gates until its acceptance criteria and authorized delivery are\n+complete. Once current-head checks and assigned reviews pass, squash merge\n+without a second confirmation. Use the available wait/monitor mechanism for\n+pending external gates; pending CI alone is not a reason to hand the task back.\n+Keep the user informed without turning progress updates into approval prompts.\n+Goal authority does not expand scope, override execution permissions or permit\n+unrelated destructive actions, releases or host/account configuration changes.\n \n 9. **Atomic Conventional Commit.** Stage only the verified, reviewed slice.\n    Use `<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>` with type `feat`, `fix`,\n@@ -117,6 +131,12 @@ requires revalidation, not abandonment of the task. Stop for missing authority,\n credentials, required user interaction or scope expansion. Do not treat an\n environment failure as a product defect or silently waive a gate.\n \n+Respect an explicit pause or resource constraint. If Actions is intentionally\n+disabled, keep it disabled until the user authorizes re-enabling it; continue\n+permitted local work and publication, but do not treat absent CI as green.\n+When required gates cannot run under that constraint, report the blocker and\n+remaining work rather than claiming completion or bypassing the merge gate.\n+\n For a CI UI failure, read the assertion and `CAKEBREW_UI_TREE_*` dump in the\n job log before calling it flaky. Rerun once only when evidence indicates\n infrastructure; otherwise fix the cause through the workflow.\n@@ -155,6 +175,13 @@ Handoffs must identify the state examined: worktree, base/head and relevant\n uncommitted file state. Include concise observed results and log/artifact paths,\n not raw log floods. A result for another tree or stale binary is not evidence.\n \n+**Parallel work is encouraged:** the primary agent should delegate independent\n+slices, investigations and gate passes concurrently when useful. Identify\n+dependencies first; do not wait for one independent slice to finish before\n+starting another. Preserve lifecycle order within each slice, and integrate\n+dependent slices in order. The primary agent coordinates shared resources,\n+collects every handoff and owns delivery; parallelism does not allow self-review.\n+\n **Safe concurrency:** use isolated worktrees for independent mutating work.\n Never change sources while a verifier or reviewer examines that workspace.\n Separate derived-data directories do not isolate the app's `NSUserDefaults`,\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"All seven skill YAML frontmatters valid\nAll five unchanged custom agents valid and routed to AGENTS.md\ndiff --git a/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md\nindex a4b2dd5..ba14938 100644\n--- a/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.agents/skills/cakebrew-deliver/SKILL.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n ---\n name: cakebrew-deliver\n-description: Deliver a verified Cakebrew slice when the user authorizes committing, publishing, opening a PR or merging; coordinate any required remediation through the workflow.\n+description: Deliver a verified Cakebrew slice under a user-assigned goal or explicit delivery request, including gated squash merge and remediation within the authorized scope.\n ---\n \n # Cakebrew Delivery\n@@ -9,4 +9,9 @@ Read the repository's `AGENTS.md` completely before acting. It is the sol