{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T02:18:11.285Z","ordinal":22467,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0229170f3e6ec7c3016a9f705dd5f487d1a69a1fb9980e0350","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ZQlKrTS0zTXZQHAKzEswPUD8","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /private/tmp/cakebrew-workflow-pr.Cx78mk/body.md\\n@@\\n-- Consolidate the engineering lifecycle and Cakebrew-specific safeguards in AGENTS.md, reducing it from 475 to 302 lines.\\n+- Consolidate the engineering lifecycle and Cakebrew-specific safeguards in AGENTS.md, reducing it from 475 to 329 lines.\\n@@\\n - Make CONTRIBUTING.md a short entry point rather than a duplicate workflow.\\n+- Explicitly authorize useful parallel delegation and continuous, in-scope goal delivery through squash merge without repeated stage approvals. Preserve explicit user limits, shared-state isolation, required checks and genuine stopping conditions.\\n@@\\n-- Six independent workflow dry runs covering CI remediation, reviewer/implementer separation, shared UI runtime, false-green tests, delivery authorization and documentation-versus-CI validation.\\n+- Initial independent workflow dry runs covered CI remediation, reviewer/implementer separation, shared UI runtime, false-green tests and documentation-versus-CI validation. Follow-up review checks the revised goal authority against green gates, explicit leave-open limits, parallel slices, paused Actions and diagnosis-only requests.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --check && shasum -a 256 .codex/config.toml workflow.md && git status --short --untracked-files=all\",max_output_tokens:900}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a07ecd-5860-7493-96ec-54998be34ff0","create_time":1788833879.185351}}}
